Thanks a lot

133
00:07:38,260 --> 00:07:39,260
I appreciate it

134
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:40,260
I appreciate it

135
00:07:40,260 --> 00:07:41,260
Huh?

136
00:07:41,260 --> 00:07:42,260
Itsuki!

137
00:07:42,260 --> 00:07:43,260
What were you up to in the staff office?

138
00:07:43,260 --> 00:07:48,260
I just had a few questions about the lecture today

139
00:07:48,260 --> 00:07:49,260
So I stopped by

140
00:07:49,260 --> 00:07:50,260
Gotcha

141
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:52,260
I was asking about the festival

142
00:07:52,260 --> 00:07:55,260
They want the class reps to take charge of everything

143
00:07:55,260 --> 00:07:56,260
Do they?

144
00:07:56,260 --> 00:07:58,260
Speaking of class reps

145
00:07:58,260 --> 00:07:59,260
Yeah

146
00:07:59,260 --> 00:08:03,260
I don't know if this kind of festival is really Iwasugi's thing

147
00:08:03,260 --> 00:08:04,260
Anyway

148
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:08,260
Apparently it's tradition for the third years to do food stalls

149
00:08:08,260 --> 00:08:10,260
Karage and frankfurters

150
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:12,260
Buttered potatoes are nice too

151
00:08:12,260 --> 00:08:13,260
I'm sorry

152
00:08:13,260 --> 00:08:16,260
I have to help out with cram school

153
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:18,260
But let's talk more about this later, okay?

154
00:08:24,260 --> 00:08:27,260
I thought Itsuki would be at least a little interested

155
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:30,260
Has everyone left already?

156
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:36,260
Need something, Yotsuba?

157
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:39,260
Sorry, didn't mean to interrupt you

158
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:41,260
It's just

159
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:44,260
The food stalls for the festival, right?

160
00:08:44,260 --> 00:08:46,260
Just give me a second, okay?

161
00:08:46,260 --> 00:08:48,260
I have no time to waste right now

162
00:08:48,260 --> 00:08:49,260
Uh, sure

163
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:50,260
Sure

164
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:54,260
What's

165
00:08:54,260 --> 00:09:11,260
Sure

166
00:09:11,260 --> 00:09:18,260
Rai-ha was telling me about that commercial Ichka was in.

167
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:32,260
Just wait. I'll make it a summer you'll never forget.

168
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:37,260
She's doing well as an actress now. Getting out there, realizing her dream.

169
00:09:37,260 --> 00:09:40,260
And Ichka's working toward becoming a teacher.

170
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:44,260
She's not cut out for it, but that's her dream.

171
00:09:44,260 --> 00:09:45,260
So, Yotsuba.

172
00:09:45,260 --> 00:09:46,260
Yes?

173
00:09:46,260 --> 00:09:50,260
Have you given any thought to what your future will hold?

174
00:09:50,260 --> 00:09:53,260
Wow, that came out of nowhere.

175
00:09:57,260 --> 00:09:59,260
I've never really considered it.

176
00:09:59,260 --> 00:10:03,260
Well, you have a great deal of talent when it comes to athletics.

177
00:10:03,260 --> 00:10:06,260
I'm sure there'll be options for you in that field.

178
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,260
I'm ready now.

179
00:10:10,260 --> 00:10:13,260
Let's go gather some intel on last year's food stalls.

180
00:10:14,260 --> 00:10:19,260
Are you sure? I mean what you said before about not having any time.

181
00:10:19,260 --> 00:10:24,260
No time to waste. It's our last big school event. I have to make it count.

182
00:10:24,260 --> 00:10:27,260
If I'm going to do this, I want to have fun in the process.

183
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:30,260
Time's a finite thing. There's never enough of it.

184
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:33,260
So I'll need your help.

185
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,260
Okay! I've got your back!

186
00:10:38,260 --> 00:10:44,260
These are the food stall items that were popular last year.

187
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:49,260
If there's something you'd like to do that's not on this list, go ahead and shout it out!

188
00:10:49,260 --> 00:10:58,260
My vote is for takoyaki. I don't see any reason to stray away from what works. And besides, you did the research for that list, didn't you?

189
00:10:58,260 --> 00:11:02,260
Nice! This'll give me the chance to show off my takoyaki skills from work.

190
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:04,260
Yes, sounds good to me as well.

191
00:11:04,260 --> 00:11:06,260
Dunno. What do you think?

192
00:11:08,260 --> 00:11:09,260
So, any other suggestions?

193
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:11,260
I want to do taiyaki!

194
00:11:11,260 --> 00:11:12,260
Bubble tea!

195
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:15,260
Miku, what would you like to do?

196
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:20,260
Pancakes, maybe?

197
00:11:20,260 --> 00:11:25,260
Well, um, there isn't any sales data on record through last year.

198
00:11:25,260 --> 00:11:26,260
It could work, though.

199
00:11:26,260 --> 00:11:28,260
Good suggestion. Thanks.

200
00:11:28,260 --> 00:11:29,260
Yeah, thanks, Miku.

201
00:11:29,260 --> 00:11:33,260
I was thinking that would be good, too. You might look so cute!

202
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:40,260
Let's leave it here for today. We'll decide another time.

203
00:11:42,260 --> 00:11:47,260
Nakano, this concert sounds cool. Do you think maybe we could be part of it?

204
00:11:47,260 --> 00:11:48,260
Yeah, of course!

205
00:11:48,260 --> 00:11:52,260
The Clothing Club's going to be presenting these. We might not get any visitors, though.

206
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,260
Oh! That's beautiful!

207
00:11:55,260 --> 00:11:59,260
We could put posters up in the designated areas. I'm happy to help you out if you'd like me to.

208
00:11:59,260 --> 00:12:00,260
Thank you so much!

209
00:12:01,260 --> 00:12:02,260
Yotsuba's so popular.

210
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:04,260
Why is no one asking for my advice?

211
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:06,260
We lose.

212
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:08,260
Are there invitations that we can send out to family?

213
00:12:09,260 --> 00:12:10,260
Absolutely!

214
00:12:11,260 --> 00:12:12,260
Invitations...

215
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,260
I'm on board with the food stall idea.

216
00:12:15,260 --> 00:12:17,260
Whatever we go with, it's going to be fun to make.

217
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:19,260
Yeah, I can't wait to start.

218
00:12:20,260 --> 00:12:21,260
You're going to be on the cooking team?

219
00:12:22,260 --> 00:12:23,260
We're going to have outside customers, you know.

220
00:12:24,260 --> 00:12:26,260
You could end up poisoning the entire neighborhood if you're not careful.

221
00:12:27,260 --> 00:12:29,260
I've gotten better, thank you very much.

222
00:12:30,260 --> 00:12:31,260
Besides, I have you.

223
00:12:32,260 --> 00:12:33,260
So I'm not worried.

224
00:12:33,260 --> 00:12:34,260
I'm not worried.

225
00:12:36,260 --> 00:12:37,260
Well, obviously.

226
00:12:37,260 --> 00:12:41,260
If I'm around to supervise, everything will go exactly the way it's supposed to.

227
00:12:42,260 --> 00:12:43,260
Thanks for waiting!

228
00:12:44,260 --> 00:12:45,260
You've been busy.

229
00:12:46,260 --> 00:12:47,260
Think maybe you're working too hard?

230
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:50,260
It's our last big school event, right?

231
00:12:50,260 --> 00:12:54,260
I want to make sure we finish the festival without any regrets.

232
00:12:59,260 --> 00:13:00,260
The last one.

233
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:02,260
Yeah.

234
00:13:03,260 --> 00:13:04,260
I appreciate this.

235
00:13:05,260 --> 00:13:08,260
I'm sure you've got plenty to do without having to help me study, too.

236
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:10,260
Do you have enough time for your college prep?

237
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,260
Seems like the festival is keeping you pretty busy.

238
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:17,260
Actually, I just got my evaluation back from my preferred school.

239
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:19,260
Really?

240
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:21,260
It's for my eyes only!

241
00:13:22,260 --> 00:13:23,260
Nobody can look at it but me!

242
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:25,260
Okay, let me guess.

243
00:13:25,260 --> 00:13:26,260
You got an A.

244
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:28,260
Well, that's no fun.

245
00:13:29,260 --> 00:13:30,260
Of course you did well.

246
00:13:30,260 --> 00:13:32,260
But that's because you're naturally studious.

247
00:13:32,260 --> 00:13:34,260
It's a lot harder for mere mortals like us.

248
00:13:35,260 --> 00:13:36,260
So please keep looking out for everyone.

249
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:38,260
We're not at the finish line yet.

250
00:13:39,260 --> 00:13:40,260
You don't need to worry.

251
00:13:41,260 --> 00:13:43,260
Everything's going to turn out exactly as it should.

252
00:13:44,260 --> 00:13:45,260
I swear, Ichka.

253
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:47,260
I'll make this the best school festival ever.

254
00:13:47,260 --> 00:13:50,260
Just admit that you're wrong, boys.

255
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:52,260
You're the ones who have it wrong.

256
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,260
I bet you couldn't find anyone who doesn't love a fluffy pancake.

257
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,260
Pack us up on this, Miku.

258
00:13:58,260 --> 00:13:59,260
Oh, well, uh...

259
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:01,260
You saw the data from last year.

260
00:14:01,260 --> 00:14:03,260
There's not a single human in this country who hates takoyaki.

261
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,260
Right, Nino?

262
00:14:06,260 --> 00:14:07,260
Yeah.

263
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,260
You said yourself that you like pancakes, Nino.

264
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:10,260
So why are you siding with them?

265
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:12,260
You didn't really mean it, right?

266
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,260
You didn't really mean it.

267
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:17,260
Okay, here's how it is, people.

268
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:19,260
I was the one who proposed takoyaki.

269
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,260
I'll take responsibility.

270
00:14:22,260 --> 00:14:23,260
