It was a perfect way to kick off the festival.

533
00:27:05,580 --> 00:27:08,440
Please don't tell me this is how you're planning to spend the rest of it.

534
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:11,900
I should be able to get it done by three.

535
00:27:12,120 --> 00:27:12,700
Don't worry.

536
00:27:14,900 --> 00:27:15,880
I'm exhausted.

537
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,500
Any idea what Fu's been up to?

538
00:27:20,320 --> 00:27:21,680
This is the building you want.

539
00:27:22,460 --> 00:27:23,860
Thank you for bringing me here.

540
00:27:24,320 --> 00:27:26,460
You seem like a very considerate young man.

541
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:29,280
Uwasugi!

542
00:27:30,520 --> 00:27:32,420
We want to turn this into a rest area.

543
00:27:32,680 --> 00:27:33,340
Think you can help?

544
00:27:34,260 --> 00:27:35,120
Uh, sure.

545
00:27:35,120 --> 00:27:43,240
Hey, I'm here.

546
00:27:44,020 --> 00:27:44,580
Miku!

547
00:27:44,760 --> 00:27:45,600
Glad you made it.

548
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:46,380
You're late.

549
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,440
Where have you been?

550
00:27:47,700 --> 00:27:48,640
Never mind that.

551
00:27:48,700 --> 00:27:50,020
We're all here now, aren't we?

552
00:27:50,600 --> 00:27:50,980
Nope.

553
00:27:51,220 --> 00:27:52,220
Still one to go.

554
00:27:54,120 --> 00:27:55,500
Hey, Ichika.

555
00:27:55,900 --> 00:27:56,840
Wow, you came!

556
00:27:57,160 --> 00:27:59,120
And you didn't bother giving us a heads up?

557
00:27:59,320 --> 00:28:01,060
Surprised you weren't mobbed by fans.

558
00:28:01,060 --> 00:28:03,520
I managed somehow.

559
00:28:03,920 --> 00:28:05,960
Now we're all present and accounted for.

560
00:28:06,360 --> 00:28:08,500
Hands down, my favorite group of people.

561
00:28:09,080 --> 00:28:09,720
I agree.

562
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,920
Wow, look at that spread.

563
00:28:12,140 --> 00:28:14,100
We bought all kinds of food from the stalls.

564
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:15,040
Finally!

565
00:28:15,280 --> 00:28:16,680
I've been waiting for this all day.

566
00:28:16,680 --> 00:28:24,880
I love you, all five of you.

567
00:28:27,780 --> 00:28:29,300
Well, that was unexpected.

568
00:28:29,540 --> 00:28:29,800
Yeah.

569
00:28:30,020 --> 00:28:31,280
And what does it even mean?

570
00:28:32,080 --> 00:28:33,560
I wish things were simpler,

571
00:28:33,820 --> 00:28:36,200
and the six of us could always be together like this,

572
00:28:36,340 --> 00:28:37,960
but we can't.

573
00:28:38,380 --> 00:28:40,500
Life's not simple, and I have to give an answer.

574
00:28:42,900 --> 00:28:45,380
Futuro, it's okay.

575
00:28:45,380 --> 00:28:46,580
Thank you.

576
00:28:48,260 --> 00:28:50,400
Of course, I'm not such an idiot

577
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,160
that I would do it in the middle of a festival.

578
00:28:53,060 --> 00:28:55,860
And to be honest, I don't quite know myself yet.

579
00:28:56,400 --> 00:28:58,020
Please, give me until the last day.

580
00:28:59,640 --> 00:29:01,160
Are you kidding with this?

581
00:29:01,460 --> 00:29:03,160
That's so anticlimactic.

582
00:29:04,040 --> 00:29:06,540
Let's get back to it, then, starting with a toast.

583
00:29:06,740 --> 00:29:07,700
I want orange juice.

584
00:29:07,720 --> 00:29:08,740
Where's the matcha soda?

585
00:29:08,820 --> 00:29:09,580
There isn't any.

586
00:29:09,900 --> 00:29:10,660
Here we are.

587
00:29:10,960 --> 00:29:12,720
You've almost got it figured out.

588
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:14,560
This has been a long road.

589
00:29:14,560 --> 00:29:16,660
Not like solving a math problem, is it?

590
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,240
You're teasing me now?

591
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:21,060
I have to admit, I am envious.

592
00:29:24,660 --> 00:29:26,260
Here, you need a drink, too.

593
00:29:26,520 --> 00:29:27,260
Oh, thank you.

594
00:29:27,260 --> 00:29:31,080
Well, then, I propose a toast

595
00:29:31,080 --> 00:29:32,740
to the first day of the festival.

596
00:29:33,700 --> 00:29:34,620
Cheers, everyone.

597
00:29:36,780 --> 00:29:39,540
Welcome all to day two of the Hinodei Festival.

598
00:29:40,440 --> 00:29:42,520
We'll be covering the action throughout the day,

599
00:29:42,600 --> 00:29:44,260
but first off, let's interview a few of the...

600
00:29:44,820 --> 00:29:46,220
Nakano, are you here?

601
00:29:46,480 --> 00:29:48,420
You do remember me from track, don't you?

602
00:29:48,660 --> 00:29:49,360
Let's meet a...

603
00:29:49,360 --> 00:29:50,800
You're still running, right?

604
00:29:51,040 --> 00:29:52,440
Hey, that's my microphone.

605
00:29:52,440 --> 00:29:53,640
I'm sorry.

606
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:54,440
I should be going.

607
00:29:54,540 --> 00:29:55,380
Come on.

608
00:29:56,280 --> 00:29:57,700
Okay, let's try again.

609
00:29:58,160 --> 00:29:59,240
Oh, hello there, ma'am.

610
00:29:59,760 --> 00:30:01,580
What brings you to the festival grounds?

611
00:30:02,040 --> 00:30:02,980
Oh, not much.

612
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:06,840
I'm here to see a childhood friend.

613
00:30:07,840 --> 00:30:09,880
There's no work for you today, Uesugi.

614
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:10,860
Huh?

615
00:30:10,860 --> 00:30:12,240
You should have fun.

616
00:30:12,640 --> 00:30:13,640
Go enjoy the festival.

617
00:30:13,820 --> 00:30:14,500
You've earned it.

618
00:30:16,340 --> 00:30:18,060
How can I enjoy it?

619
00:30:18,300 --> 00:30:20,080
I didn't even bring money for food.

620
00:30:21,680 --> 00:30:24,200
Oh, I know somewhere I can go.

621
00:30:26,120 --> 00:30:27,200
There you are.

622
00:30:27,680 --> 00:30:29,600
Hutano, you've grown up a lot.

623
00:30:33,720 --> 00:30:34,600
Takebayashi!

624
00:30:36,820 --> 00:30:38,960
Wow, you're terrible at this game.

625
00:30:38,960 --> 00:30:41,200
Try aiming it further to the right.

626
00:30:41,380 --> 00:30:43,240
I'm just missing because you're bugging me.

627
00:30:43,460 --> 00:30:45,420
Oh, hey, do you see that one back there?

628
00:30:45,680 --> 00:30:46,560
Win it for me, would you?

629
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:52,460
So after all those nice things Futuro said yesterday,

630
00:30:52,820 --> 00:30:54,440
he's out on a date with another girl.

631
00:30:54,980 --> 00:30:55,980
Looks that way.

632
00:30:56,760 --> 00:30:58,500
Uesugi's a popular guy, I guess.

633
00:30:58,920 --> 00:31:00,240
Futuro, over here.

634
00:31:00,360 --> 00:31:01,240
Okay, okay.

635
00:31:05,960 --> 00:31:07,740
Fresh pancakes, nice and hot.

636
00:31:07,840 --> 00:31:08,440
Look, Futuro.

637
00:31:08,760 --> 00:31:09,920
They're selling pancakes.

638
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:10,960
Let's get some.

639
00:31:11,300 --> 00:31:11,920
Oh, yeah.

640
00:31:12,300 --> 00:31:14,300
The girls in my class are running this one.

641
00:31:15,460 --> 00:31:16,260
Who's that?

642
00:31:16,840 --> 00:31:19,360
I appreciate you girls for taking care of my Futuro.

643
00:31:19,980 --> 00:31:20,760
Hold on, Mai.

644
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:22,700
I don't believe we've met.

645
00:31:22,900 --> 00:31:23,860
It's nice to meet you.

646
00:31:24,280 --> 00:31:25,440
My name is Takebayashi.

647
00:31:25,940 --> 00:31:28,480
Futuro and I were in the same class in elementary school.

648
00:31:28,800 --> 00:31:29,720
Is that so?

649
00:31:29,900 --> 00:31:32,920
Well, he happens to be in the same high school class as me and all my sisters.

650
00:31:33,240 --> 00:31:36,660
Though I think we're too involved in his life to refer to ourselves as just classmates.

651
00:31:36,660 --> 00:31:38,560
Wow, what a wonderful coincidence.

652
00:31:39,200 --> 00:31:41,820
Would you believe I used to help Futuro with schoolwork too?

653
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:46,220
He was always such a troublemaker, so I was pretty shocked when he asked me to tutor him.

654
00:31:46,460 --> 00:31:47,000
No, no.

655
00:31:47,120 --> 00:31:48,540
I'm the one doing the tutoring.

656
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:50,180
Oh, I understand.

657
00:31:50,660 --> 00:31:52,120
Well, that explains everything then.

658
00:31:52,840 --> 00:31:56,020
So out of all of us, now we know who's closest to him.

659
00:31:57,760 --> 00:31:59,320
Yotspa, this is too much.

660
00:31:59,560 --> 00:32:00,000
I...

661
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:04,280
Uasuki means more to me than you could...

662
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,480
That's very sweet of you.

663
00:32:05,800 --> 00:32:10,980
If you taught him a long time ago, then I guess you could say that we're sort of indebted to you in a roundabout way.

664
00:32:11,840 --> 00:32:15,040
Technically, you're the person who spent the most time around Uasuki.

665
00:32:16,420 --> 00:32:19,840
Although, the quality of the time spent is what really matters.

666
00:32:19,840 --> 00:32:24,620
Come on. You guys are starting to embarrass me.

667
00:32:26,040 --> 00:32:28,940
Ease up, Takebayashi. Stop messing with them.

668
00:32:29,420 --> 00:32:33,780
I don't have many friends, and all of these girls mean a lot to me.

669
00:32:36,480 --> 00:32:38,280
You've grown up a lot, haven't you?

670
00:32:39,200 --> 00:32:40,380
I'm sorry, you two.

671
00:32:41,040 --> 00:32:42,860
Could I order one pancake, please?

672
00:32:43,300 --> 00:32:44,060
Um, it's dripping.

673
00:32:44,700 --> 00:32:45,220
Yotspa?

674
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:48,400
I'm fine. Sorry, I should get back to work.

675
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:52,600
Look, Fu.

676
00:32:53,020 --> 00:32:56,340
I want you to know that my feelings about you haven't changed.

677
00:33:02,520 --> 00:33:04,300
You're back. Good talk?

678
00:33:04,660 --> 00:33:06,940
Yeah. I think Futado's doing well.

679
00:33:07,180 --> 00:33:09,200
And the quintuplets are great girls, too.

680
00:33:09,540 --> 00:33:10,760
Huh? Quintuplets?

681
00:33:13,220 --> 00:33:15,240
Give it your best, Futado.

682
00:33:18,400 --> 00:33:28,200
Was this the right choice?

683
00:33:28,740 --> 00:33:32,220
Or was it wrong to even make a choice like this in the first place?

684
00:33:33,500 --> 00:33:36,380
Three days was nowhere near enough time to figure that out.

685
00:33:37,100 --> 00:33:39,940
Sadly, three days was all I had.

686
00:33:39,940 --> 00:33:52,800
This concludes the Asahi High School Festival.

687
00:33:53,700 --> 00:33:56,560
The after party, and all of our scheduled programming.

688
00:33:56,560 --> 00:34:03,660
The taxi's running late.

689
00:34:05,040 --> 00:34:05,860
Hey, Futado.

690
00:34:05,940 --> 00:34:08,960
By the way, I heard Ichika Nakano goes to this high school, too.

691
00:34:09,260 --> 00:34:10,460
Oh, man, I love her.

692
00:34:10,720 --> 00:34:12,600
She was really gorgeous in that drama.

693
00:34:13,020 --> 00:34:13,420
Ooh!

694
00:34:13,420 --> 00:34:16,780
I'd love to do a kissing scene like that if it was with her.

695
00:34:18,020 --> 00:34:18,460
Hmm.

696
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:22,340
Are you disappointed to hear I did a kissing scene?

697
00:34:22,580 --> 00:34:22,980
No.

698
00:34:23,180 --> 00:34:24,080
I'm an actress.

699
00:34:24,340 --> 00:34:25,800
It's part of the job sometimes.

700
00:34:26,060 --> 00:34:27,160
That's not the point.

701
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:30,480
I guess not, since you've already had your first kiss anyway.

702
00:34:31,360 --> 00:34:31,840
Wait!

703
00:34:32,040 --> 00:34:33,000
How did you know that?

704
00:34:33,460 --> 00:34:34,580
It was an accident.

705
00:34:34,580 --> 00:34:37,420
Oh, so you actually have.

706
00:34:37,620 --> 00:34:38,420
Uh...

707
00:34:38,420 --> 00:34:39,900
All right, who'd you kiss?

708
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:41,580
Um, I still don't know.

709
00:34:41,880 --> 00:34:44,140
All five of you were dressed like Ichiki that day.

710
00:34:44,860 --> 00:34:45,340
Hmm.

711
00:34:46,160 --> 00:34:48,140
Well, who'd you think it was?

712
00:34:49,720 --> 00:34:50,520
Uh...

713
00:34:50,520 --> 00:34:53,740
The taxi's here.

714
00:34:54,320 --> 00:34:55,760
You lucked out this time.

715
00:34:59,560 --> 00:35:03,300
Hey, there's a chance I won't be able to go to the school festival.

716
00:35:03,300 --> 00:35:06,160
So, could I ask you for your answer now?

717
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:06,540
Hmm?

718
00:35:06,820 --> 00:35:09,280
Um, but it's okay if you haven't decided yet.

719
00:35:09,320 --> 00:35:09,660
Listen.

720
00:35:11,620 --> 00:35:13,140
I choose none of you.

721
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:14,660
That's my answer.

722
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:24,080
How dare you!

723
00:35:24,260 --> 00:35:26,040
Get yourself together or you'll be sorry!

724
00:35:26,480 --> 00:35:27,040
Sorry!

725
00:35:27,620 --> 00:35:28,480
And cut!

726
00:35:28,740 --> 00:35:29,540
Great job!

727
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:30,840
Exactly what I wanted!

728
00:35:30,840 --> 00:35:33,020
Um, I hope you're not hurt.

729
00:35:33,300 --> 00:35:34,140
Is it me?

730
00:35:34,360 --> 00:35:35,800
Or are you used to this?

731
00:35:41,760 --> 00:35:42,600
Ah...

732
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:44,300
Another good day of work.

733
00:35:44,680 --> 00:35:46,420
Time to go relax at the hotel.

734
00:35:46,760 --> 00:35:47,700
Ichika, there you are!

735
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:48,420
Is something wrong?

736
00:35:48,860 --> 00:35:50,080
I just got a phone call.

737
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:52,120
They said that your sister collapsed.

738
00:35:52,120 --> 00:35:52,460
Ah!

739
00:35:57,340 --> 00:35:59,180
Seems like you're feeling a bit better.

740
00:35:59,660 --> 00:36:00,720
Take it easy, okay?

741
00:36:00,720 --> 00:36:01,220
Uh...

742
00:36:01,220 --> 00:36:05,540
Nino!

743
00:36:06,060 --> 00:36:06,460
Futaro!

744
00:36:07,460 --> 00:36:08,760
Didn't think you were coming.

745
00:36:09,260 --> 00:36:09,580
Yeah.

746
00:36:10,020 --> 00:36:12,840
I called, but I couldn't stop worrying till I came by.

747
00:36:13,220 --> 00:36:14,280
How's everyone else?

748
00:36:14,560 --> 00:36:15,160
Not bad.

749
00:36:15,380 --> 00:36:16,840
They're getting settled in right now.

750
00:36:17,140 --> 00:36:18,480
But don't worry about us.

751
00:36:18,780 --> 00:36:20,080
I promise we'll be okay.

752
00:36:20,640 --> 00:36:21,340
All right, then.

753
00:36:21,560 --> 00:36:22,160
That's good.

754
00:36:22,160 --> 00:36:26,460
I need to head back to the campus to do some more cleaning.

755
00:36:27,180 --> 00:36:29,300
You guys might as well walk each other home, right?

756
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:30,460
Uh, okay.

757
00:36:31,460 --> 00:36:33,700
Well then, guess I'll call it a day now.

758
00:36:35,780 --> 00:36:36,780
Actually, hold on.

759
00:36:37,140 --> 00:36:38,540
Are you done with everything, too?

760
00:36:38,980 --> 00:36:39,320
Yeah.

761
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:40,360
Great!

762
00:36:40,460 --> 00:36:41,700
Then we should go for a walk.

763
00:36:41,700 --> 00:36:48,500
This place is pretty spread out, huh?

764
00:36:49,220 --> 00:36:50,960
Remember last time we came here?

765
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:53,080
Yeah, for the fireworks festival.

766
00:36:55,320 --> 00:36:58,580
It feels a little empty without the booths and people around.

767
00:36:58,580 --> 00:37:03,520
It's not completely deserted, though.

768
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:04,140
Mm-hmm.

769
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:08,760
You know, it's pretty common for couples to start dating at this festival.

770
00:37:09,380 --> 00:37:12,260
Especially during the big after-party when the third day's over.

771
00:37:12,800 --> 00:37:16,040
I figured maybe you knew that, and that was why you said what you did.

772
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:16,640
Heh.

773
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:20,540
You've known me way too long to think I'm the type who keeps up with stuff like that.

774
00:37:20,720 --> 00:37:21,920
Oh, come on now.

775
00:37:22,300 --> 00:37:25,080
Sometimes you do stoop to the level of us regular people.

776
00:37:25,240 --> 00:37:25,480
Huh?

777
00:37:25,580 --> 00:37:26,040
How so?

778
00:37:26,200 --> 00:37:28,260
I've seen you peek inside expensive cars.

779
00:37:28,580 --> 00:37:30,880
You get crazy excited when you go on vacation.

780
00:37:31,200 --> 00:37:33,020
You like to shout from the top of a mountain.

781
00:37:33,380 --> 00:37:34,760
You noticed all that?

782
00:37:35,080 --> 00:37:35,480
Uh-huh.

783
00:37:35,760 --> 00:37:37,800
Just a few of the things that make you so cute.

784
00:37:39,340 --> 00:37:42,140
You should value those sincere feelings more.

785
00:37:42,500 --> 00:37:42,680
Huh?

786
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:46,720
So please, stop saying that you aren't choosing anyone.

787
00:37:47,100 --> 00:37:49,400
But I still don't know for sure how I feel.

788
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:54,500
Either you're overthinking all of this, or you're just avoiding thinking about it.

789
00:37:54,960 --> 00:37:56,440
Remember our talk about kissing?

790
00:37:56,440 --> 00:38:00,260
Out of Nino, Miku, Yotsuba, and Itsuki.

791
00:38:00,880 --> 00:38:01,660
Be honest.

792
00:38:02,160 --> 00:38:05,020
Who would you have been the happiest to find out it was?

793
00:38:07,840 --> 00:38:08,780
Just kidding.

794
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,620
Oh, a fending machine.

795
00:38:11,000 --> 00:38:12,160
Go get yourself something.

796
00:38:12,260 --> 00:38:13,020
It's my treat.

797
00:38:14,160 --> 00:38:16,460
Pick whatever drink sounds good to you.

798
00:38:17,120 --> 00:38:17,580
What?

799
00:38:17,580 --> 00:38:19,520
I'll be waiting on the bench.

800
00:38:19,920 --> 00:38:21,140
What are you doing?

801
00:38:22,920 --> 00:38:23,980
By the way!

802
00:38:24,600 --> 00:38:29,620
Black tea's Nino, green's Miku, juice's Yotsuba, and canned coffee is Itsuki.

803
00:38:30,340 --> 00:38:31,940
Uh-that's not fair.

804
00:38:32,700 --> 00:38:33,980
I had to do something.

805
