1045
00:55:28,820 --> 00:55:34,140
who's that girl tell me what girl back at the shooting game

1046
00:55:34,140 --> 00:55:37,560
oh we were friends as kids do you like her

1047
00:55:37,560 --> 00:55:40,760
like in that way uh she's just a friend

1048
00:55:40,760 --> 00:55:45,700
oh good i'm relieved i've been resisting the urge to ask you

1049
00:55:45,700 --> 00:55:51,220
you have really you don't need to hold back for my sake you know

1050
00:55:51,220 --> 00:55:56,440
in that case i want to kiss you

1051
00:55:56,440 --> 00:56:00,760
i know i told you not to hold back but how do we end up here

1052
00:56:00,760 --> 00:56:03,100
i guess i can ask you for your answer again later

1053
00:56:03,100 --> 00:56:11,260
no matter how high a wall stands in my way

1054
00:56:11,260 --> 00:56:15,960
as long as i believe in myself i know i can cross over it

1055
00:56:15,960 --> 00:56:34,280
this concludes the asahi high school festival the after party and all of our scheduled programming

1056
00:56:34,280 --> 00:56:42,500
thanks i hope you enjoy

1057
00:56:42,500 --> 00:56:45,940
oh no queen emerald

1058
00:56:45,940 --> 00:56:48,080
it's over for you heroes

1059
00:56:48,080 --> 00:56:50,880
though i would prefer not to slay you where you stand

1060
00:56:50,880 --> 00:56:52,960
so i order you to join my forces

1061
00:56:52,960 --> 00:57:00,380
i was so worried it wouldn't work out

1062
00:57:00,380 --> 00:57:03,800
i can't thank you enough for covering the role for me nakano

1063
00:57:03,800 --> 00:57:06,840
sure anytime always happy to make myself useful

1064
00:57:06,840 --> 00:57:09,480
i'm here to perform the safety inspection

1065
00:57:09,480 --> 00:57:10,760
oh yeah thanks

1066
00:57:10,760 --> 00:57:13,540
looks like their ingredients meet the expectations

1067
00:57:13,540 --> 00:57:19,220
you should clean up those paper scraps in case they catch fire

1068
00:57:19,220 --> 00:57:23,060
at this rate i think i'll be done by 3 p.m

1069
00:57:23,060 --> 00:57:25,080
step right up

1070
00:57:25,080 --> 00:57:27,640
thanks for helping us advertise

1071
00:57:27,640 --> 00:57:29,640
here i want to give you a coupon

1072
00:57:29,640 --> 00:57:33,280
i can't wait to try it

1073
00:57:33,280 --> 00:57:42,160
so tired

1074
00:57:42,160 --> 00:57:45,480
you did a great job today

1075
00:57:45,480 --> 00:57:50,120
you're not built for all this physical labor

1076
00:57:50,120 --> 00:57:51,440
you should go take a break

1077
00:57:51,440 --> 00:57:54,780
i'm fine but thanks anyway

1078
00:57:54,780 --> 00:57:58,340
can i get through i'm trying to finish this by 3

1079
00:57:58,340 --> 00:58:00,860
i'm worried about you

1080
00:58:00,860 --> 00:58:03,160
i'm not letting you go until you listen to me

1081
00:58:03,160 --> 00:58:09,880
right i guess i haven't eaten since this morning

1082
00:58:09,880 --> 00:58:12,040
with all these food options around

1083
00:58:12,040 --> 00:58:14,060
well at least it's an easy fix

1084
00:58:14,060 --> 00:58:18,700
go get some karaage and regain your strength

1085
00:58:18,700 --> 00:58:20,780
you're sure you don't want this

1086
00:58:20,780 --> 00:58:23,380
uh-huh i'm totally full so i don't need it

1087
00:58:23,380 --> 00:58:27,260
that was just because i'm still digesting

1088
00:58:27,260 --> 00:58:29,360
now let's get these moved

1089
00:58:29,360 --> 00:58:32,260
yotsuba thank you for this

1090
00:58:32,260 --> 00:58:34,760
i'm lucky that you're around

1091
00:58:34,760 --> 00:58:36,860
oh come on don't make it a big deal

1092
00:58:36,860 --> 00:58:38,880
we help each other out all the time don't we

1093
00:58:38,880 --> 00:58:40,960
to be honest

1094
00:58:40,960 --> 00:58:43,080
no matter how tough things get

1095
00:58:43,080 --> 00:58:45,380
it was suki's approval makes it all worth it

1096
00:58:45,380 --> 00:58:48,640
two more days till he answers us

1097
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:52,900
after that we probably won't have to carry on like this anymore

1098
00:58:52,900 --> 00:58:58,100
but if he ends up choosing me then

1099
00:58:58,100 --> 00:59:06,960
damn it it's not fair we've all worked so hard

1100
00:59:06,960 --> 00:59:10,000
and now we have to close up shop on day two

1101
00:59:10,000 --> 00:59:12,740
i mean they did warn us that it would be dangerous

1102
00:59:12,740 --> 00:59:15,700
after an incident like that there really isn't anything else we can do

1103
00:59:15,700 --> 00:59:17,080
shit

1104
00:59:17,080 --> 00:59:25,400
can i work here

1105
00:59:25,400 --> 00:59:27,360
is there anything you need

1106
00:59:27,360 --> 00:59:37,460
oh i know you you're futaro's friend

1107
00:59:37,460 --> 00:59:47,100
where am i on campus

1108
00:59:47,100 --> 00:59:51,660
the hospital trust me i was just as surprised as you are

1109
00:59:51,660 --> 00:59:54,280
you haven't been taking care of yourself at all

1110
00:59:54,280 --> 00:59:57,280
nino i'm sorry for worrying you

1111
00:59:57,280 --> 00:59:58,880
i'll be right back

1112
00:59:58,880 --> 01:00:01,260
there's still a lot i have to do for the festival

1113
01:00:01,260 --> 01:00:03,600
wait i need to hurry

1114
01:00:03,600 --> 01:00:05,780
the drama club is depending on me

1115
01:00:05,780 --> 01:00:07,760
yotsuba it's night time

1116
01:00:07,760 --> 01:00:10,540
the second day's over already

1117
01:00:10,540 --> 01:00:16,660
the girl futaro met

1118
01:00:16,660 --> 01:00:18,760
that time six years ago

1119
01:00:18,760 --> 01:00:19,800
it was you right

1120
01:00:19,800 --> 01:00:21,080
you know

1121
01:00:21,080 --> 01:00:22,880
how could i not

1122
01:00:22,880 --> 01:00:24,920
he showed me your picture so many times

1123
01:00:24,920 --> 01:00:25,900
it drove me crazy

1124
01:00:25,900 --> 01:00:29,440
i talked to your sisters over at the pancake stand about it

1125
01:00:29,440 --> 01:00:31,840
they told me you got lost that day

1126
01:00:31,840 --> 01:00:35,420
and he helped you i think i see why you were usuki's teacher

1127
01:00:35,420 --> 01:00:38,340
i just wanted to say i'm glad i met you

1128
01:00:38,340 --> 01:00:40,240
have you told futaro you were

1129
01:00:40,240 --> 01:00:41,300
please don't tell him

1130
01:00:41,300 --> 01:00:42,820
why shouldn't i

1131
01:00:42,820 --> 01:00:46,080
because he'll be disappointed

1132
01:00:46,080 --> 01:00:49,560
usuki's been working so hard during these six years

1133
01:00:49,560 --> 01:00:52,200
and i just obsessed over stupid things

1134
01:00:52,200 --> 01:00:53,960
and problems that don't matter

1135
01:00:53,960 --> 01:00:56,460
instead of helping out

1136
01:00:56,460 --> 01:00:58,440
i've caused people trouble

1137
01:00:58,440 --> 01:01:00,840
i don't serve any purpose at all

1138
01:01:00,840 --> 01:01:02,640
that's really what you think

1139
01:01:02,640 --> 01:01:08,480
i know someone who felt like they were worthless

1140
01:01:08,480 --> 01:01:10,300
and that no one needed them

1141
01:01:10,300 --> 01:01:11,900
the same as you do

1142
01:01:11,900 --> 01:01:14,420
it took a long time

1143
01:01:14,420 --> 01:01:16,640
but that person's moving forward with life now

1144
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:19,880
i hope you can learn how to leave your past behind too

1145
01:01:19,880 --> 01:01:21,520
oh you're up

1146
01:01:21,520 --> 01:01:23,340
please so wasuki

1147
01:01:23,340 --> 01:01:24,600
let me get by you

1148
01:01:24,600 --> 01:01:25,920
i have some stuff to do

1149
01:01:25,920 --> 01:01:27,720
i kind of doubt that

1150
01:01:27,720 --> 01:01:29,720
everyone's already gone home

1151
01:01:29,720 --> 01:01:31,960
then i'll go door to door and apologize

1152
01:01:31,960 --> 01:01:34,560
you don't understand

1153
01:01:34,560 --> 01:01:36,240
it's not just the drama club

1154
01:01:36,240 --> 01:01:39,100
i promised a lot of people i'd help them today

1155
01:01:39,100 --> 01:01:40,820
and then i went and let them down

1156
01:01:40,820 --> 01:01:42,680
this is all my fault

1157
01:01:42,680 --> 01:01:44,140
i failed again

1158
01:01:44,140 --> 01:01:46,380
i won't let you leave

1159
01:01:46,380 --> 01:01:50,020
you've been prescribed absolute bed rest

1160
01:01:50,020 --> 01:01:52,520
i plan to make sure you get it

1161
01:01:52,520 --> 01:01:54,980
sit down and relax

1162
01:01:54,980 --> 01:01:56,820
and while you do

1163
01:01:56,820 --> 01:02:00,120
i'll catch you up on everything that happened during the festival

1164
01:02:00,120 --> 01:02:02,080
it's over for you

1165
01:02:02,080 --> 01:02:03,460
so stop right there

1166
01:02:03,460 --> 01:02:05,400
wait a sec

1167
01:02:05,400 --> 01:02:07,520
that was the captain of the track team

1168
01:02:07,520 --> 01:02:09,720
yeah she jumped in there and covered for you

1169
01:02:09,720 --> 01:02:12,180
apparently she watched the whole show yesterday

1170
01:02:12,180 --> 01:02:15,300
but that costume was tailored to fit my measurements

1171
01:02:15,300 --> 01:02:17,480
do you remember these two

1172
01:02:17,480 --> 01:02:20,440
they're from the clothing club

1173
01:02:20,440 --> 01:02:23,100
don't tell me they had to alter it last minute

1174
01:02:23,100 --> 01:02:25,120
it's all my fault

1175
01:02:25,120 --> 01:02:26,980
a lot of people stepped up

1176
01:02:26,980 --> 01:02:32,800
you get it now

1177
01:02:32,800 --> 01:02:35,980
it's not because you did something wrong

1178
01:02:35,980 --> 01:02:38,260
they want to be there for you

1179
01:02:38,260 --> 01:02:42,760
you help out all the time

1180
01:02:42,760 --> 01:02:43,340
don't you

1181
01:02:43,340 --> 01:02:46,140
it's okay if you ask for help once in a while

1182
01:02:46,140 --> 01:02:47,840
let me handle it

1183
01:02:47,840 --> 01:02:50,760
since you've always been there for me

1184
01:02:50,760 --> 01:02:53,380
uasuki

1185
01:02:53,380 --> 01:02:57,280
i feel so terrible for all the trouble i've caused everyone

1186
01:02:57,280 --> 01:02:58,780
so please

1187
01:02:58,780 --> 01:03:02,460
can you make sure the last day goes well in my place

1188
01:03:02,460 --> 01:03:04,460
yeah leave it to me

1189
01:03:04,460 --> 01:03:17,840
futara uasugi

1190
01:03:17,840 --> 01:03:22,700
long time to see rena

1191
01:03:22,700 --> 01:03:25,460
sorry but i had a long day today

1192
01:03:25,460 --> 01:03:27,520
could you come by later

1193
01:03:27,520 --> 01:03:31,040
thank you for remembering our promise

1194
01:03:31,040 --> 01:03:33,840
even though i couldn't keep up my end of it

1195
01:03:33,840 --> 01:03:36,540
forgive me

1196
01:03:36,540 --> 01:03:39,160
you don't need to worry about that

1197
01:03:39,160 --> 01:03:40,480
are you sure though

1198
01:03:40,480 --> 01:03:41,620
doesn't it bother you

1199
01:03:41,620 --> 01:03:42,760
i mean

1200
01:03:42,760 --> 01:03:45,620
the past doesn't matter as much as the present

1201
01:03:45,620 --> 01:03:47,120
so no

1202
01:03:47,120 --> 01:03:55,040
i'll stop focusing on our past so much

1203
01:03:55,040 --> 01:03:58,400
i'm going to find my own place in this world

1204
01:03:58,400 --> 01:03:59,780
so

1205
01:03:59,780 --> 01:04:02,120
this is it

1206
01:04:02,120 --> 01:04:18,040
talk about an embarrassing dream

1207
01:04:18,040 --> 01:04:21,040
must have been everything that happened at the festival

1208
01:04:21,040 --> 01:04:29,420
i can't believe i went for it

1209
01:04:29,420 --> 01:04:31,360
i hope he doesn't mind

1210
01:04:31,360 --> 01:04:34,180
it's the last memory we'll have together

1211
01:04:34,180 --> 01:04:37,660
but it's time for me to stop lingering in the past

1212
01:04:37,660 --> 01:04:39,460
i think now

1213
01:04:39,460 --> 01:04:42,300
i'll finally be able to move on

1214
01:04:42,300 --> 01:04:43,240
yeah

1215
01:04:43,240 --> 01:04:44,920
i can

1216
01:04:44,920 --> 01:05:02,460
this concludes the asahi high school festival

1217
01:05:02,460 --> 01:05:04,100
the after party

1218
01:05:04,100 --> 01:05:06,300
and all of our scheduled programming

1219
01:05:06,300 --> 01:05:16,300
i know you

1220
01:05:16,300 --> 01:05:21,020
you've done so much for me mr muto

1221
01:05:21,020 --> 01:05:22,080
thanks a lot

1222
01:05:22,080 --> 01:05:23,560
look at you

1223
01:05:23,560 --> 01:05:27,100
it takes a diligent student to be hitting the books during a festival

1224
01:05:27,100 --> 01:05:28,080
thank you

1225
01:05:28,080 --> 01:05:29,180
i mean

1226
01:05:29,180 --> 01:05:32,200
i'm hoping to get into college and become a teacher

1227
01:05:32,200 --> 01:05:35,340
i'm following in my mother's footsteps

1228
01:05:35,340 --> 01:05:38,620
oh she was a high school teacher i forgot to say

1229
01:05:38,620 --> 01:05:39,700
i know

1230
01:05:39,700 --> 01:05:43,740
i was her homeroom teacher back when she was in high school

1231
01:05:43,740 --> 01:05:45,280
in fact

1232
01:05:45,280 --> 01:05:47,700
you look a lot like she did when she was younger

1233
01:05:47,700 --> 01:05:49,120
do you mean that

1234
01:05:49,120 --> 01:05:50,740
yes

1235
01:05:50,740 --> 01:05:52,880
it's almost uncanny

1236
01:05:52,880 --> 01:05:57,560
her admiration for me was part of the reason she pursued a teaching career

1237
01:05:57,560 --> 01:06:01,320
and she regretted that decision until the very end

1238
01:06:01,320 --> 01:06:03,600
in my life

1239
01:06:03,600 --> 01:06:06,180
i've made so many mistakes

1240
01:06:06,180 --> 01:06:10,360
if you're planning to be a teacher just emulate her

1241
01:06:10,360 --> 01:06:12,260
then i'm against it

1242
01:06:12,260 --> 01:06:14,420
by the way

1243
01:06:14,420 --> 01:06:16,860
i heard there was a fire at one of the stalls

1244
01:06:16,860 --> 01:06:19,720
yeah there was but luckily nobody got hurt

1245
01:06:19,720 --> 01:06:21,040
well that's good to hear

1246
01:06:21,040 --> 01:06:23,720
i wanted to ask you

1247
01:06:23,720 --> 01:06:26,380
did you notice a strange old man at the festival

1248
01:06:26,380 --> 01:06:27,160
huh

1249
01:06:27,160 --> 01:06:28,360
oh that's right

1250
01:06:28,360 --> 01:06:30,740
dad was kind of obsessing over this all day long

1251
01:06:30,740 --> 01:06:32,660
he's bald and has a beard

1252
01:06:32,660 --> 01:06:34,000
it's gray

1253
01:06:34,000 --> 01:06:35,520
and kind of fluffy too

1254
01:06:35,520 --> 01:06:36,440
yeah

1255
01:06:36,440 --> 01:06:40,200
with the kind of face that would look the same if you turned it upside down

1256
01:06:40,200 --> 01:06:42,540
so he was there

1257
01:06:42,540 --> 01:06:45,340
why are you asking about him

1258
01:06:45,340 --> 01:06:48,580
i should probably tell you this in case something happens

1259
01:06:48,580 --> 01:06:50,960
that man is

1260
01:06:50,960 --> 01:06:54,240
what can i do for you sir

1261
01:06:54,240 --> 01:06:58,200
i have something to confess and i think this may be the time to say it

1262
01:06:58,200 --> 01:07:00,580
your mother was a student of mine

1263
01:07:00,580 --> 01:07:02,700
we were colleagues for a while

1264
01:07:02,700 --> 01:07:03,920
and then

1265
01:07:03,920 --> 01:07:06,460
she became my wife

1266
01:07:06,460 --> 01:07:08,380
in other words

1267
01:07:08,380 --> 01:07:10,700
i'm your biological father

1268
01:07:10,700 --> 01:07:11,860
father

1269
01:07:11,860 --> 01:07:14,180
yes

1270
01:07:14,180 --> 01:07:15,700
i've missed you itsuki

1271
01:07:15,700 --> 01:07:18,980
for my work as an instructor i've traveled all over japan

1272
01:07:18,980 --> 01:07:22,000
and i've thought about you girls every step of the way

1273
01:07:22,000 --> 01:07:23,460
then one day

1274
01:07:23,460 --> 01:07:25,940
i happened to see ichika in a commercial

1275
01:07:25,940 --> 01:07:29,040
i'd like to make up for lost time

1276
01:07:29,040 --> 01:07:30,380
no you're too late

1277
01:07:30,380 --> 01:07:33,280
i remember everything that mom told us about you

1278
01:07:33,280 --> 01:07:35,900
the moment you heard she was going to have quintuplets

1279
01:07:35,900 --> 01:07:36,940
you left her

1280
01:07:36,940 --> 01:07:38,120
and that was it

1281
01:07:38,120 --> 01:07:39,800
how could you

1282
01:07:39,800 --> 01:07:42,000
do you have any idea how she felt

1283
01:07:42,000 --> 01:07:43,400
you're no father

1284
01:07:43,400 --> 01:07:45,780
i'm sorry

1285
01:07:45,780 --> 01:07:48,260
please give me a chance to make things right

1286
01:07:48,260 --> 01:07:49,720
even if it's too late

1287
01:07:49,720 --> 01:07:52,220
i want to at least do what i can as a parent

1288
01:07:52,220 --> 01:07:53,340
well

1289
01:07:53,340 --> 01:07:55,880
the truth is we already have a dad

1290
01:07:55,880 --> 01:07:58,360
you can be on your way now

1291
01:07:58,360 --> 01:08:00,480
do you mean nakano

1292
01:08:00,480 --> 01:08:02,380
after your mother passed away

1293
01:08:02,380 --> 01:08:04,860
did he really do anything good for you girls

1294
01:08:04,860 --> 01:08:09,900
face it itsuki you're wasting time chasing after your mother's ghost

1295
01:08:09,900 --> 01:08:14,000
and i can't bear to watch my daughter make the same mistake she did

1296
01:08:14,000 --> 01:08:18,480
i know without a doubt that teaching is the wrong career for you

1297
01:08:18,480 --> 01:08:21,440
and i think there's a part of you that knows it as well

1298
01:08:21,440 --> 01:08:26,280
as a father i can't allow you to go down this path

1299
01:08:26,280 --> 01:08:29,620
i love my daughters why else would i be here

1300
01:08:29,620 --> 01:08:34,720
it's key

1301
01:08:34,720 --> 01:08:35,600
yeah

1302
01:08:35,600 --> 01:08:37,200
is she okay

1303
01:08:37,200 --> 01:08:39,080
has she been acting differently

1304
01:08:39,080 --> 01:08:42,060
i haven't seen her since yesterday so i'm not sure

1305
01:08:42,060 --> 01:08:43,000
what happened

1306
01:08:43,000 --> 01:08:45,160
your biological father's here

1307
01:08:45,160 --> 01:08:47,800
and i think he's been in contact with her

1308
01:08:47,800 --> 01:08:48,320
oh no

1309
01:08:48,320 --> 01:08:49,620
really

1310
01:08:49,620 --> 01:08:56,720
it's key hasn't been around

1311
01:08:56,720 --> 01:08:58,880
today's the last day too

1312
01:08:58,880 --> 01:09:00,620
i wonder what's wrong

1313
01:09:00,620 --> 01:09:03,100
she hasn't left her room for the entire day

1314
01:09:03,100 --> 01:09:04,460
i see

1315
01:09:04,460 --> 01:09:06,460
hold it

1316
01:09:06,460 --> 01:09:09,100
you're going to her place right

1317
01:09:09,100 --> 01:09:10,560
take this with you

1318
01:09:10,560 --> 01:09:11,880
are you sure

1319
01:09:11,880 --> 01:09:14,100
that's just what i like about you fu

1320
01:09:14,100 --> 01:09:15,660
always consider it

1321
01:09:15,660 --> 01:09:17,620
leave the rest to me okay

1322
01:09:17,620 --> 01:09:19,580
please take care of itsuki

1323
01:09:19,580 --> 01:09:30,160
what's that

1324
01:09:30,160 --> 01:09:32,320
wasuki

1325
01:09:32,320 --> 01:09:34,860
i have no idea what i'm doing

1326
01:09:34,860 --> 01:09:37,100
is all of this a mistake

1327
01:09:37,100 --> 01:09:40,480
don't let what that old geezer said get to you

1328
01:09:40,480 --> 01:09:42,800
he was obviously just talking out of his ass

1329
01:09:42,800 --> 01:09:44,100
i know what mom would say

1330
01:09:44,100 --> 01:09:45,640
itsuki

1331
01:09:45,640 --> 01:09:48,140
you shouldn't grow up to be like me

1332
01:09:48,140 --> 01:09:49,800
i never wanted that for you

1333
01:09:49,800 --> 01:09:54,400
and yet i won't change my mind

1334
01:09:54,400 --> 01:09:57,360
i'm still aspiring to become like she was

1335
01:09:57,360 --> 01:10:00,180
because it's what i want

1336
01:10:00,180 --> 01:10:02,020
is that so awful of me

1337
01:10:02,020 --> 01:10:04,800
well one thing's for sure

1338
01:10:04,800 --> 01:10:07,480
there's nothing that great about becoming a teacher

1339
01:10:07,480 --> 01:10:11,420
not every student has potential you know

1340
01:10:11,420 --> 01:10:15,580
in fact you'll learn really quickly that some people are just irreparably stupid

1341
01:10:15,580 --> 01:10:17,820
but you have to work with them

1342
01:10:17,820 --> 01:10:19,920
so you've got to pretend that's not true

1343
01:10:19,920 --> 01:10:24,880
investing in other people is a surefire way to wear out your mind and body

1344
01:10:24,880 --> 01:10:28,360
then there are some students who will be rebellious

1345
01:10:28,360 --> 01:10:30,120
and you can't run away

1346
01:10:30,120 --> 01:10:32,580
you have to dig your heels in and fight

1347
01:10:32,580 --> 01:10:36,540
take it from someone who knows it's a real pain in the ass

1348
01:10:36,540 --> 01:10:39,460
becoming a teacher is a terrible idea

1349
01:10:39,460 --> 01:10:41,380
but that isn't the point

1350
01:10:41,380 --> 01:10:44,060
you can't let some stranger control your life

1351
01:10:44,060 --> 01:10:45,460
this is your dream

1352
01:10:45,460 --> 01:10:47,460
no matter how difficult it is

1353
01:10:47,460 --> 01:10:50,980
you're the only one who gets to decide if it's worth it or not

1354
01:10:50,980 --> 01:10:53,860
but is becoming a teacher actually my dream

1355
01:10:53,860 --> 01:10:56,580
all i want is to be like my mother

1356
01:10:56,580 --> 01:11:00,580
at least that's what somebody told me once

1357
01:11:00,580 --> 01:11:03,320
chasing a dream to be like her

1358
01:11:03,320 --> 01:11:06,460
that's not the same as being like her by chasing a dream

1359
01:11:06,460 --> 01:11:09,700
as long as you're living your own life

1360
01:11:09,700 --> 01:11:13,620
admiring your mother and aspiring to be more like her

1361
01:11:13,620 --> 01:11:14,920
isn't a bad thing

1362
01:11:14,920 --> 01:11:16,740
in that case

1363
01:11:16,740 --> 01:11:20,800
i want to become a great teacher like my mother

1364
01:11:20,800 --> 01:11:24,460
and i'm going to teach because it's what i want to do

1365
01:11:24,460 --> 01:11:27,500
if that's what you're after

1366
01:11:27,500 --> 01:11:30,580
then as your tutor there's only one thing for me to do

1367
01:11:30,580 --> 01:11:33,820
i'll support you it's key completely

1368
01:11:33,820 --> 01:11:35,340
oh suki

1369
01:11:35,340 --> 01:11:38,940
then i have the perfect idea

1370
01:11:38,940 --> 01:11:43,700
will you help me study

1371
01:11:43,700 --> 01:11:46,500
i'd love to

1372
01:11:46,500 --> 01:11:48,820
i appreciate it

1373
01:11:48,820 --> 01:11:50,780
but before we begin

1374
01:11:50,780 --> 01:11:57,320
there's something important that i need to do

1375
01:11:57,320 --> 01:12:03,640
excuse me mr muda

1376
01:12:03,640 --> 01:12:05,320
hey there

1377
01:12:05,320 --> 01:12:10,060
i have to say i wasn't expecting you to come and talk to me

1378
01:12:10,060 --> 01:12:15,060
i take it you finally come to your senses and decided to listen to your father

1379
01:12:15,060 --> 01:12:16,680
right

1380
01:12:16,680 --> 01:12:20,080
her father huh

1381
01:12:20,080 --> 01:12:21,360
you're kidding me

1382
01:12:21,360 --> 01:12:23,080
it's you

1383
01:12:23,080 --> 01:12:24,000
yep

1384
01:12:24,000 --> 01:12:25,920
it's been a long time teach

1385
01:12:25,920 --> 01:12:29,340
honestly i would have been fine with never seeing you again

1386
01:12:29,340 --> 01:12:33,000
hello there muda

1387
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:35,060
how have you been

1388
01:12:35,060 --> 01:12:36,120
nakano

1389
01:12:36,120 --> 01:12:39,940
i'm happy i have a chance to apologize to you

1390
01:12:39,940 --> 01:12:42,960
after all i left you with a terrible burden

1391
01:12:42,960 --> 01:12:46,500
and i'm sorry

1392
01:12:46,500 --> 01:12:47,720
no

1393
01:12:47,720 --> 01:12:50,000
actually i'm grateful to you

1394
01:12:50,000 --> 01:12:55,680
if it wasn't for you and your self-serving behavior my five daughters and i would have never been brought together

1395
01:12:55,680 --> 01:12:57,280
is that so

1396
01:12:57,280 --> 01:13:02,060
because from where i'm standing it doesn't look like you've kept up with all your responsibilities either

1397
01:13:02,060 --> 01:13:05,540
which is why when poor little itski needed her father's help

1398
01:13:05,540 --> 01:13:07,280
she couldn't depend on you

1399
01:13:07,280 --> 01:13:08,760
so she came to see me

1400
01:13:08,760 --> 01:13:10,640
itski's here as well

1401
01:13:10,640 --> 01:13:13,720
what are you talking about

1402
01:13:13,720 --> 01:13:16,380
look carefully

1403
01:13:16,380 --> 01:13:19,180
and you'll see this isn't itski

1404
01:13:19,180 --> 01:13:24,680
i've been over here the whole time

1405
01:13:24,680 --> 01:13:27,020
what are you girls doing

1406
01:13:27,020 --> 01:13:28,360
i deceived you

1407
01:13:28,360 --> 01:13:29,260
i'm sorry

1408
01:13:29,260 --> 01:13:32,260
but i had to confirm what i already knew would happen

1409
01:13:32,260 --> 01:13:33,980
it's just a mistake

1410
01:13:33,980 --> 01:13:36,200
what point are you trying to prove here

1411
01:13:36,200 --> 01:13:38,960
if you really loved us then you could tell us apart

1412
01:13:38,960 --> 01:13:41,480
that's what our mom said

1413
01:13:41,480 --> 01:13:45,940
when will you stop bringing up your mother and her absurd ideas

1414
01:13:45,940 --> 01:13:49,780
there's nothing good that will come of you trying to emulate a delusional woman

1415
01:13:49,780 --> 01:13:52,160
if you really want to follow in her footsteps

1416
01:13:52,160 --> 01:13:54,400
don't you think she'd rather you let this go

1417
01:13:54,400 --> 01:13:57,020
don't fixate on such silly things

1418
01:13:57,020 --> 01:14:02,420
she used to tell us about the choices in life that she regretted

1419
01:14:02,420 --> 01:14:03,260
that's right

1420
01:14:03,260 --> 01:14:04,740
she made a lot of mistakes

1421
01:14:04,740 --> 01:14:07,220
we both know she wouldn't want her daughter to do the same

1422
01:14:07,220 --> 01:14:09,040
sorry but you're wrong about that

1423
01:14:09,040 --> 01:14:11,660
one thing i know is

1424
01:14:11,660 --> 01:14:14,300
even if she felt like she did everything wrong

1425
01:14:14,300 --> 01:14:16,140
i would still disagree with her

1426
01:14:16,140 --> 01:14:17,820
and that's my right

1427
01:14:17,820 --> 01:14:19,760
because my mom and i are different

1428
01:14:19,760 --> 01:14:22,460
she gave her all for us

1429
01:14:22,460 --> 01:14:24,980
anyone could see how deeply she cared

1430
01:14:24,980 --> 01:14:26,520
she was so kind

1431
01:14:26,520 --> 01:14:31,060
and there's no way it could be a mistake for a person to live their life like that

1432
01:14:31,060 --> 01:14:33,880
what would a child like you know about living

1433
01:14:33,880 --> 01:14:37,180
you're the one who's raving and shouting about something you don't understand

1434
01:14:37,180 --> 01:14:40,740
you didn't see the hope and faith she had in her children

1435
01:14:40,740 --> 01:14:42,420
after all how could you

1436
01:14:42,420 --> 01:14:43,640
you weren't there

1437
01:14:43,640 --> 01:14:47,100
in fact you have no right to speak of her at all

1438
01:14:47,100 --> 01:14:49,020
dad's never

1439
01:14:49,020 --> 01:14:51,380
mr. muto

1440
01:14:51,380 --> 01:14:53,520
you walked out on mom

1441
01:14:53,520 --> 01:14:56,360
and you never even bothered apologizing to her

1442
01:14:56,360 --> 01:15:00,040
you're not getting my forgiveness either

1443
01:15:00,040 --> 01:15:02,300
i won't let you use me to ease your guilt

1444
01:15:02,300 --> 01:15:05,480
you'll be haunted by what you did to her for the rest of your life

1445
01:15:05,480 --> 01:15:08,920
how dare you say that

1446
01:15:08,920 --> 01:15:11,460
this is pathetic old man

1447
01:15:11,460 --> 01:15:17,620
get lost

1448
01:15:17,620 --> 01:15:23,660
so did that take care of everything

1449
01:15:23,660 --> 01:15:28,040
let me guess you were watching us from afar weren't you

1450
01:15:28,040 --> 01:15:28,920
maybe

1451
01:15:28,920 --> 01:15:31,580
i'm really grateful to you uesugi

1452
01:15:31,580 --> 01:15:35,200
ever since mom passed away

1453
01:15:35,200 --> 01:15:36,900
i've been trying to become her

1454
01:15:36,900 --> 01:15:39,420
hoping to fill the void that she left behind

1455
01:15:39,420 --> 01:15:41,500
at some point

1456
01:15:41,500 --> 01:15:45,020
the line between my identity and hers started to blur

1457
01:15:45,020 --> 01:15:49,200
before long the faith i used to have in my dreams was wavering

1458
01:15:49,200 --> 01:15:54,400
but now i know i don't have to forget my mom

1459
01:15:54,400 --> 01:15:59,360
you're the one who taught me that you know

1460
01:15:59,360 --> 01:16:01,860
thanks uesugi

1461
01:16:01,860 --> 01:16:08,940
i just noticed the sunset really early today huh

1462
01:16:08,940 --> 01:16:10,940
guess winter's on its way

1463
01:16:10,940 --> 01:16:16,100
what's with you

1464
01:16:16,100 --> 01:16:17,380
did i say something funny

1465
01:16:17,380 --> 01:16:18,680
you're being so creepy

1466
01:16:18,680 --> 01:16:20,000
it's a personal thing

1467
01:16:20,000 --> 01:16:20,840
sorry

1468
01:16:20,840 --> 01:16:21,700
well anyway

1469
01:16:21,700 --> 01:16:25,100
i'm a lot more confident these days and i owe that to you

1470
01:16:25,100 --> 01:16:27,140
mom and i are different people

1471
01:16:27,140 --> 01:16:29,660
that's obvious but i couldn't see it

1472
01:16:29,660 --> 01:16:31,320
not till you showed me

1473
01:16:31,320 --> 01:16:36,000
my image of the perfect teacher is still my mother but

1474
01:16:36,000 --> 01:16:37,960
but what

1475
01:16:37,960 --> 01:16:39,700
i mean

1476
01:16:39,700 --> 01:16:41,000
what to say

1477
01:16:41,000 --> 01:16:42,900
the point is

1478
01:16:42,900 --> 01:16:45,940
that i think of you as perfect too

1479
01:16:45,940 --> 01:16:49,160
and i just wanted you to know that

1480
01:16:49,160 --> 01:16:52,700
and now

1481
01:16:52,700 --> 01:16:55,160
the winner for the best selling shop is

1482
01:16:55,160 --> 01:16:58,200
we did it

1483
01:16:58,200 --> 01:17:07,540
did everything go okay

1484
01:17:07,540 --> 01:17:10,300
did you tell futaro what you wanted to tell him

1485
01:17:10,300 --> 01:17:11,040
yeah

1486
01:17:11,040 --> 01:17:13,560
and i thanked him for that thing with her father

1487
01:17:13,560 --> 01:17:16,240
i meant to thank you all for that too

1488
01:17:16,240 --> 01:17:17,840
don't worry about it

1489
01:17:17,840 --> 01:17:20,740
it wouldn't be right if we didn't help with a family situation

1490
01:17:20,740 --> 01:17:22,320
true but still

1491
01:17:22,320 --> 01:17:24,320
i'm glad you did

1492
01:17:24,320 --> 01:17:25,980
so thanks okay

1493
01:17:25,980 --> 01:17:29,340
you really had to make this awkward didn't you

1494
01:17:29,340 --> 01:17:30,020
seriously

1495
01:17:30,020 --> 01:17:31,520
you helped a lot

1496
01:17:31,520 --> 01:17:32,740
and miku

1497
01:17:32,740 --> 01:17:34,240
thank you for posing as me

1498
01:17:34,240 --> 01:17:35,040
anytime

1499
01:17:35,040 --> 01:17:36,180
besides

1500
01:17:36,180 --> 01:17:38,740
i need more chances to perfect my performance

1501
01:17:38,740 --> 01:17:41,180
this is about to become a weird obsession for you

1502
01:17:41,180 --> 01:17:42,080
i can feel it

1503
01:17:42,080 --> 01:17:45,480
it was more than enough to fool someone who doesn't know us

1504
01:17:45,480 --> 01:17:47,280
even though we're pretty different

1505
01:17:47,280 --> 01:17:48,720
our faces are still the same

1506
01:17:48,720 --> 01:17:49,320
yep

1507
01:17:49,320 --> 01:17:53,980
i wonder if we'll always be the matching set we are now

1508
01:17:53,980 --> 01:18:00,160
but you know what

1509
01:18:00,160 --> 01:18:02,720
there's lots of time before we meet up with futaro

1510
01:18:02,720 --> 01:18:05,520
let's forget all that and enjoy the after party

1511
01:18:05,520 --> 01:18:07,160
guys

1512
01:18:07,160 --> 01:18:10,220
how long are we gonna sit here wasting the day away

1513
01:18:10,220 --> 01:18:12,620
why don't we go get some food from the stalls huh

1514
01:18:12,620 --> 01:18:13,920
all right the stalls

1515
01:18:13,920 --> 01:18:15,260
forgot about them

1516
01:18:15,260 --> 01:18:17,520
i guess i haven't eaten in a while

1517
01:18:17,520 --> 01:18:19,980
and there was a shop that i didn't see yet

1518
01:18:19,980 --> 01:18:22,260
but after we do that i gotta go

1519
01:18:22,260 --> 01:18:24,620
i'm supposed to meet up with somebody

1520
01:18:24,620 --> 01:18:26,260
oh i get it

1521
01:18:26,260 --> 01:18:28,580
that's right i saw the nakano sisters earlier

1522
01:18:28,580 --> 01:18:30,280
i know ichiko was there

1523
01:18:30,280 --> 01:18:31,520
it might have been all five of them

1524
01:18:31,520 --> 01:18:32,740
that's onnaida

1525
01:18:32,740 --> 01:18:36,020
i'm surprised you knew which one was ichiko right away

1526
01:18:36,020 --> 01:18:38,340
yeah i did

1527
01:18:38,340 --> 01:18:40,220
this is gonna sound weird

1528
01:18:40,220 --> 01:18:43,280
but i can always tell ichiko apart from the rest of the girls

1529
01:18:43,280 --> 01:18:46,180
and you can identify all five can't you uesugi

1530
01:18:46,180 --> 01:18:46,940
uh

1531
01:18:46,940 --> 01:18:47,720
huh

1532
01:18:47,720 --> 01:18:50,480
now that you mention it i'm not really sure

1533
01:18:50,480 --> 01:18:52,880
first it was nearly impossible

1534
01:18:52,880 --> 01:18:55,780
i'm not good at remembering faces to start with

1535
01:18:55,780 --> 01:19:00,680
the worst part is they constantly take advantage of that fact

1536
01:19:00,680 --> 01:19:03,940
you have no idea how many times they pulled one over on me

1537
01:19:03,940 --> 01:19:07,120
they'll be a pain until the bitter end

1538
01:19:07,120 --> 01:19:09,180
yeah it sucks to be you

1539
01:19:09,180 --> 01:19:11,340
i have a question by the way

1540
01:19:11,340 --> 01:19:15,180
which one of the girls was the first one you were able to tell apart flawlessly

1541
01:19:15,180 --> 01:19:19,820
hey how about those stalls

1542
01:19:19,820 --> 01:19:22,640
not so fast

1543
01:19:22,640 --> 01:19:24,140
i want to hear the answer

1544
01:19:24,140 --> 01:19:26,640
why are you torturing the poor guy takeda

1545
01:19:26,640 --> 01:19:29,940
because i think uesugi might be keeping a little secret from us

1546
01:19:29,940 --> 01:19:31,700
there's nothing to tell you

1547
01:19:31,700 --> 01:19:33,840
then why are you in such a rush to get away

1548
01:19:33,840 --> 01:19:36,240
friends aren't supposed to keep secrets you know

1549
01:19:36,240 --> 01:19:38,640
forget it no comment all right

1550
01:19:38,640 --> 01:19:40,980
i know what it is

1551
01:19:40,980 --> 01:19:42,840
you like one of them don't you

1552
01:19:42,840 --> 01:19:48,640
a student's job is to study

1553
01:19:48,640 --> 01:19:52,140
for years i felt like that was all that mattered

1554
01:19:52,140 --> 01:19:56,400
but no there's no reason to cut everything else out of my life

1555
01:19:56,400 --> 01:20:00,840
studying friendship work fun relationships

1556
01:20:00,840 --> 01:20:04,340
those girls do everything to the fullest

1557
01:20:04,340 --> 01:20:09,400
i was so stuck in my ways until they came along and taught me how to live

1558
01:20:09,400 --> 01:20:13,940
i just wish i hadn't kept them waiting for so long while i was getting it through my head

1559
01:20:13,940 --> 01:20:20,240
if they hadn't changed me for the better i would probably still be alone to this day

1560
01:20:20,240 --> 01:20:31,740
but what's the point of shopping around if you didn't bring money with you

1561
01:20:31,740 --> 01:20:34,240
the resting area is a total lifesaver huh

1562
01:20:34,240 --> 01:20:34,740
yeah

1563
01:20:34,740 --> 01:20:40,640
why wouldn't i i want to enjoy the festival until the very end

1564
01:20:40,640 --> 01:20:47,240
okay it's almost time now

1565
01:20:47,240 --> 01:21:05,840
oh sookie when today's events are over

1566
01:21:05,840 --> 01:21:08,640
we'll each be waiting for you in our rooms

1567
01:21:08,640 --> 01:21:11,120
with our own thoughts and feelings

1568
01:21:11,120 --> 01:21:12,880
hoping that you'll show up

1569
01:21:12,880 --> 01:21:21,140
but sadly you'll have to choose only one of those rooms to visit

1570
01:21:21,140 --> 01:21:28,060
we realize that this idea is going to cause a lot of heartache for you and for us

1571
01:21:28,060 --> 01:21:30,620
but this is what we've decided to do

1572
01:21:30,620 --> 01:21:34,700
we sincerely hope you understand

1573
01:21:34,700 --> 01:21:35,700
iwasuki

1574
01:21:35,700 --> 01:21:42,660
this concludes the asahi high school festival

1575
01:21:42,660 --> 01:21:44,320
the after party

1576
01:21:44,320 --> 01:21:46,520
and all of our scheduled programming

1577
01:21:46,520 --> 01:22:02,960
so you've made your choice

1578
01:22:02,960 --> 01:22:04,400
you figured it out

1579
01:22:04,400 --> 01:22:05,680
good job frutero

1580
01:22:05,680 --> 01:22:15,460
it's over now

1581
01:22:15,460 --> 01:22:21,440
when we talked that night

1582
01:22:21,440 --> 01:22:23,420
you had already decided

1583
01:22:23,420 --> 01:22:36,560
this is just the start

1584
01:22:36,560 --> 01:22:36,580
this is just the start

1585
01:22:36,580 --> 01:22:37,840
wasuki

1586
01:22:37,840 --> 01:22:46,440
there it is

1587
01:22:46,440 --> 01:22:48,020
hey

1588
01:22:48,020 --> 01:22:55,200
took me a while huh

1589
01:22:55,200 --> 01:22:58,980
what's going on what are you doing here

1590
01:22:58,980 --> 01:23:01,680
I came to see you. What else?

1591
01:23:03,340 --> 01:23:05,380
Really? You're kidding, right?

1592
01:23:07,620 --> 01:23:10,820
No, it can't be. No way this is happening.

1593
01:23:11,580 --> 01:23:14,320
I get it. I'm surprised I did this, too.

1594
01:23:15,260 --> 01:23:17,600
Also, did you have to make me wait so long?

1595
01:23:18,140 --> 01:23:19,560
Why weren't you in your room?

1596
01:23:20,360 --> 01:23:23,660
Because I was positive you'd go to someone else instead.

1597
01:23:24,220 --> 01:23:26,300
These were fresh when I bought them, you know.

1598
01:23:26,960 --> 01:23:28,080
Hey, is that...

1599
01:23:28,080 --> 01:23:29,920
You gave me the coupon, remember?

1600
01:23:30,500 --> 01:23:31,940
Here, have some.

1601
01:23:32,940 --> 01:23:34,980
You waited here for a long time.

1602
01:23:35,280 --> 01:23:38,380
Well, yeah, because I was hoping we could eat these together.

1603
01:23:45,120 --> 01:23:47,460
So, anyway, I, uh...

1604
01:23:47,460 --> 01:23:51,000
I need to make sure we're both on the same page now that you know how I feel.

1605
01:23:51,540 --> 01:23:52,420
Do you want to...

1606
01:23:52,420 --> 01:23:53,400
Sorry, but no!

1607
01:23:53,400 --> 01:23:53,900
No!

1608
01:23:53,900 --> 01:23:53,960
No!

1609
01:23:58,080 --> 01:23:58,420
Hello?

1610
01:23:59,200 --> 01:23:59,740
Uasuki?

1611
01:24:00,620 --> 01:24:02,820
Uh, is anybody in there?

1612
01:24:04,080 --> 01:24:06,320
I worked up a lot of courage to come here.

1613
01:24:06,700 --> 01:24:08,520
Wasn't expecting such a quick answer.

1614
01:24:10,720 --> 01:24:16,000
Listen, I'm really honored you chose me and everything, so I hope you don't take this the wrong way.

1615
01:24:16,000 --> 01:24:20,360
I don't think you should settle for someone like me, Uasuki.

1616
01:24:20,440 --> 01:24:23,080
I guarantee you there are plenty of girls who'd be better for you.

1617
01:24:24,680 --> 01:24:26,120
Why would you say that?

1618
01:24:26,300 --> 01:24:28,860
Well, I mean, look at my sisters.

1619
01:24:29,000 --> 01:24:30,220
Any one of them would...

1620
01:24:30,220 --> 01:24:31,280
Stop, Yotsuba.

1621
01:24:31,280 --> 01:24:36,000
I'm not asking any of your sisters.

1622
01:24:37,140 --> 01:24:39,400
I'm here to find out how you feel.

1623
01:24:43,400 --> 01:24:44,300
Come back!

1624
01:24:44,300 --> 01:24:53,080
She got away.

1625
01:24:53,800 --> 01:24:54,400
Uasuki.

1626
01:24:56,220 --> 01:24:58,380
Itsuki, where is everyone?

1627
01:24:58,700 --> 01:24:59,720
Run, that way.

1628
01:25:00,100 --> 01:25:01,320
That's where Yotsuba went.

1629
01:25:02,280 --> 01:25:04,460
You don't need to know anything else right now, okay?

1630
01:25:06,380 --> 01:25:08,920
Worrying about us four will only cause more pain.

1631
01:25:08,920 --> 01:25:12,260
Yeah, you're right.

1632
01:25:13,340 --> 01:25:13,820
Sorry.

1633
01:25:17,460 --> 01:25:20,160
There was something you always used to say, Yotsuba.

1634
01:25:20,980 --> 01:25:23,540
In fact, you said it so much that it got annoying.

1635
01:25:24,820 --> 01:25:27,500
Let's make sure we don't leave camp with any regrets.

1636
01:25:27,900 --> 01:25:31,260
So this time, let's make sure we all walk away without any regrets, okay?

1637
01:25:31,260 --> 01:25:35,140
I want to make sure we finish the festival without any regrets.

1638
01:25:35,620 --> 01:25:37,560
I'm not giving up now!

1639
01:25:38,920 --> 01:25:45,580
Get back here!

1640
01:25:45,840 --> 01:25:47,660
I'm so sorry, Uasuki.

1641
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:50,660
But I've accepted that I can't be special.

1642
01:25:51,160 --> 01:25:53,180
Because I don't deserve to be.

1643
01:25:57,180 --> 01:25:58,340
You guys!

1644
01:25:58,680 --> 01:25:59,760
Where'd you go?

1645
01:26:01,880 --> 01:26:02,400
Ow!

1646
01:26:04,740 --> 01:26:06,260
Oh no, I'm sorry.

1647
01:26:06,600 --> 01:26:07,260
It's fine.

1648
01:26:07,420 --> 01:26:08,740
I should have been paying attention.

1649
01:26:08,920 --> 01:26:10,020
It was my fault.

1650
01:26:11,680 --> 01:26:13,660
Uh-oh, it's getting really late.

1651
01:26:14,080 --> 01:26:16,200
Yeah, I guess we should take the bus home, huh?

1652
01:26:16,840 --> 01:26:17,120
Huh?

1653
01:26:17,540 --> 01:26:17,760
Hmm?

1654
01:26:18,940 --> 01:26:19,880
I can't.

1655
01:26:19,900 --> 01:26:22,420
I'm all out of money after buying that good luck charm earlier.

1656
01:26:22,980 --> 01:26:24,000
Are you stupid?

1657
01:26:24,540 --> 01:26:27,820
I only have 200 yen on me, and that's not enough for the both of us.

1658
01:26:28,300 --> 01:26:29,260
Guess you're stuck here.

1659
01:26:29,260 --> 01:26:30,360
Yeah, I'll be fine.

1660
01:26:30,360 --> 01:26:31,660
Yeah, I'll be fine.

1661
01:26:32,080 --> 01:26:33,220
Have a good night, okay?

1662
01:26:33,220 --> 01:26:34,220
Mm-hmm.

1663
01:26:42,220 --> 01:26:43,680
Look at that, it's gone.

1664
01:26:44,960 --> 01:26:48,400
My family's real poor, so I only get 5 yen for allowance.

1665
01:26:48,800 --> 01:26:49,580
That's lame, huh?

1666
01:26:49,580 --> 01:26:52,940
Aren't you sad that you don't have very much money, Futuro?

1667
01:26:54,140 --> 01:26:54,860
I don't know.

1668
01:26:54,960 --> 01:26:55,500
What do you mean?

1669
01:26:55,920 --> 01:26:57,460
That's how my family is, too.

1670
01:26:58,180 --> 01:27:01,900
My mom has to work really hard all by herself so she can take care of us.

1671
01:27:02,300 --> 01:27:05,760
To be honest, sometimes I feel like...

1672
01:27:05,760 --> 01:27:09,520
Maybe life would be a little bit better for my mom if I wasn't around, you know?

1673
01:27:10,120 --> 01:27:11,040
That's not true.

1674
01:27:11,300 --> 01:27:15,860
So I decided I'm going to study as hard as I can, and I'll become really smart.

1675
01:27:16,180 --> 01:27:18,860
Then one day I can get a job where I'll earn lots of money.

1676
01:27:19,180 --> 01:27:20,980
That'll make everything easier for her.

1677
01:27:21,720 --> 01:27:25,920
If I do that, then there'll finally be a reason for me to be here.

1678
01:27:26,580 --> 01:27:27,380
Wow, cool.

1679
01:27:28,180 --> 01:27:29,700
You're like a real grown-up.

1680
01:27:30,080 --> 01:27:30,720
All right.

1681
01:27:31,720 --> 01:27:33,360
I'm gonna study hard like you are.

1682
01:27:33,360 --> 01:27:36,340
If I get smarter, I bet I can find a great job.

1683
01:27:36,600 --> 01:27:39,760
And then I'll be super rich and things will be better for my little sister.

1684
01:27:40,160 --> 01:27:42,320
Maybe that's the way you make yourself important.

1685
01:27:45,060 --> 01:27:46,000
Let's do it.

1686
01:27:46,440 --> 01:27:46,880
Together.

1687
01:27:47,700 --> 01:27:49,700
I'll try my best for my mom's sake.

1688
01:27:50,140 --> 01:27:52,040
And you can do it to help your little sister.

1689
01:27:52,460 --> 01:27:53,860
We'll study like crazy.

1690
01:27:58,500 --> 01:27:58,940
Yeah.

1691
01:27:59,780 --> 01:28:00,220
Hey.

1692
01:28:01,000 --> 01:28:03,060
Why don't we make it official with a wish?

1693
01:28:03,360 --> 01:28:04,860
For a hundred yen a piece?

1694
01:28:04,860 --> 01:28:07,100
Yotsuba.

1695
01:28:24,620 --> 01:28:24,980
Yotsuba.

1696
01:28:26,980 --> 01:28:27,700
That ribbon.

1697
01:28:28,200 --> 01:28:29,220
It looks good on you.

1698
01:28:30,160 --> 01:28:31,340
Thanks a lot, Mom.

1699
01:28:31,840 --> 01:28:34,440
Maybe now people can tell me apart from my sisters.

1700
01:28:35,080 --> 01:28:36,500
Well, that's doubtful.

1701
01:28:37,720 --> 01:28:39,980
What you wear doesn't make much difference.

1702
01:28:40,300 --> 01:28:41,620
There's more to you than that.

1703
01:28:41,820 --> 01:28:43,040
It's not just the ribbon.

1704
01:28:43,500 --> 01:28:45,280
I study a lot more than they do.

1705
01:28:45,600 --> 01:28:47,640
And I got first place the other day, too.

1706
01:28:48,720 --> 01:28:49,820
See, Mom, I'm winning.

1707
01:28:50,300 --> 01:28:52,840
I'm so far ahead of everyone else in every way.

1708
01:28:53,120 --> 01:28:54,520
I'm not the same anymore.

1709
01:28:54,980 --> 01:28:56,240
Mom, look at these.

1710
01:28:57,060 --> 01:28:58,140
Do you like them?

1711
01:28:58,860 --> 01:29:00,260
Yes, they're very cute.

1712
01:29:00,860 --> 01:29:03,120
I changed my hair just like Yotsuba did.

1713
01:29:04,060 --> 01:29:06,920
Yotsuba, it's wonderful that you're giving your all.

1714
01:29:07,480 --> 01:29:08,740
Working hard is a good thing.

1715
01:29:09,740 --> 01:29:11,920
But, dear, you don't have to compete.

1716
01:29:12,480 --> 01:29:14,880
Each one of you is special in your own unique way.

1717
01:29:14,880 --> 01:29:20,980
As your mother, I want you girls to stay close the rest of your lives.

1718
01:29:21,920 --> 01:29:24,040
But you should always remember one thing.

1719
01:29:24,660 --> 01:29:27,040
What matters is that the five of you are together.

1720
01:29:27,900 --> 01:29:28,980
Wherever you may be.

1721
01:29:28,980 --> 01:29:39,200
I always believed she was going to get better, but she never did.

1722
01:29:41,800 --> 01:29:42,880
Pardon me, children.

1723
01:29:42,880 --> 01:29:53,520
I suppose we've never been particularly close.

1724
01:29:55,900 --> 01:29:59,360
But from now on, I'm going to be the one looking after you.

1725
01:29:59,360 --> 01:30:04,000
Mom, we just started middle school this year.

1726
01:30:04,740 --> 01:30:08,440
But there's no way the five of us can stick together the way we used to.

1727
01:30:10,520 --> 01:30:14,260
We may look alike, but we can't be the same anymore.

1728
01:30:14,260 --> 01:30:16,520
Hey, Dad, guess what?

1729
01:30:17,160 --> 01:30:18,340
Look at my test score.

1730
01:30:18,600 --> 01:30:20,520
I did the best out of all five of us.

1731
01:30:20,960 --> 01:30:21,800
That's wonderful.

1732
01:30:22,400 --> 01:30:25,060
Oh, and the track team asked me to join, but I turned them down.

1733
01:30:25,300 --> 01:30:28,300
After all, I gotta be responsible and put my studies first, right?

1734
01:30:28,680 --> 01:30:30,700
Of course. Keep up the good work.

1735
01:30:34,480 --> 01:30:36,280
He was kind of cold, huh?

1736
01:30:36,720 --> 01:30:38,940
Mom would have praised me a lot more than that.

1737
01:30:40,940 --> 01:30:42,820
She would have praised me, right?

1738
01:30:44,260 --> 01:30:48,800
I wonder if Futuro's still studying this late at night.

1739
01:30:50,560 --> 01:30:52,880
You sure you don't need this anymore, Yotsuba?

1740
01:30:53,480 --> 01:30:56,200
Nah, I need to focus on school anyways.

1741
01:30:56,560 --> 01:30:58,560
Okay, then maybe I'll borrow it.

1742
01:31:00,500 --> 01:31:02,760
Awesome, it's improving a little every time.

1743
01:31:03,140 --> 01:31:04,600
I just have to keep on pushing.

1744
01:31:05,380 --> 01:31:06,200
Hey, Yotsuba.

1745
01:31:06,940 --> 01:31:09,460
My history grade, it's gotten way better.

1746
01:31:10,580 --> 01:31:12,440
It's because of that game you lent me.

1747
01:31:13,720 --> 01:31:14,140
Wow.

1748
01:31:14,760 --> 01:31:15,100
Really?

1749
01:31:15,760 --> 01:31:16,920
That's great, Miku.

1750
01:31:18,800 --> 01:31:20,220
I need to work harder.

1751
01:31:20,920 --> 01:31:22,280
I'll study all I can.

1752
01:31:22,820 --> 01:31:24,400
Then I'll become really smart.

1753
01:31:24,940 --> 01:31:27,980
That way, I can work for a company that pays me lots.

1754
01:31:27,980 --> 01:31:32,240
I still failed.

1755
01:31:32,240 --> 01:31:34,560
What's the point of studying, then?

1756
01:31:34,560 --> 01:31:35,940
You don't need to be special.

1757
01:31:35,940 --> 01:31:39,940
What's important is that the five of you remain together.

1758
01:31:39,940 --> 01:31:42,600
Why does it matter if we're all together?

1759
01:31:42,600 --> 01:31:43,600
I don't understand what you mean.

1760
01:31:43,600 --> 01:31:45,260
I don't understand what you mean.

1761
01:31:45,260 --> 01:31:46,260
I don't need to be special.

1762
01:31:46,260 --> 01:31:47,140
I don't need to be special.

1763
01:31:47,140 --> 01:31:47,920
I don't need to be special.

1764
01:31:47,920 --> 01:31:48,920
I don't need to be special.

1765
01:31:48,920 --> 01:31:49,920
I don't need to be special.

1766
01:31:49,920 --> 01:31:50,920
I don't need to be special.

1767
01:31:50,920 --> 01:31:51,920
I don't need to be special.

1768
01:31:51,920 --> 01:31:54,420
I'm selected to run in the interscholastic meet.

1769
01:31:54,420 --> 01:31:55,420
Well done.

1770
01:31:55,420 --> 01:31:57,080
Are you watching, Mom?

1771
01:31:57,080 --> 01:31:58,080
Mom.

1772
01:31:58,080 --> 01:31:59,540
The whole room is praising me.

1773
01:31:59,540 --> 01:32:05,680
There's a lot of people who need me, and it's because I'm me, not because I'm one of the

1774
01:32:05,680 --> 01:32:06,580
Nakano sisters.

1775
01:32:06,580 --> 01:32:09,580
You've been training really hard recently.

1776
01:32:09,580 --> 01:32:12,100
Listen, how are your grades?

1777
01:32:12,100 --> 01:32:15,320
I can always help you with your homework if you want me to.

1778
01:32:15,320 --> 01:32:17,920
I'm different from the rest of you now.

1779
01:32:19,920 --> 01:32:21,280
I'm not like you.

1780
01:32:22,360 --> 01:32:23,180
That's right.

1781
01:32:23,740 --> 01:32:25,200
I'm the best of the sisters.

1782
01:32:25,720 --> 01:32:26,640
I'm special.

1783
01:32:27,080 --> 01:32:32,740
You've had two make-up exams now, and you've failed both of them, which means you'll repeat

1784
01:32:32,740 --> 01:32:33,740
your grade.

1785
01:32:36,580 --> 01:32:37,580
Is that true?

1786
01:32:37,580 --> 01:32:38,580
No way.

1787
01:32:38,580 --> 01:32:39,580
You're joking.

1788
01:32:39,580 --> 01:32:40,580
No.

1789
01:32:40,580 --> 01:32:41,580
This isn't a joke.

1790
01:32:41,580 --> 01:32:46,580
But ma'am, I've been doing so well in my club, and on the basketball team.

1791
01:32:46,580 --> 01:32:48,580
None of those things matter.

1792
01:32:48,580 --> 01:32:53,240
I gave you plenty of warning, Miss Nakano, and yet you continued trying to join every club

1793
01:32:53,240 --> 01:32:54,840
that you could find.

1794
01:32:54,840 --> 01:32:55,720
Gather your belongings.

1795
01:32:55,720 --> 01:32:57,220
Thanks.

1796
01:32:59,220 --> 01:33:00,220
A transfer?

1797
01:33:00,220 --> 01:33:04,720
Luckily, I have a contact who's on the executive board at a coeducational school.

1798
01:33:04,720 --> 01:33:09,220
I'll send you there when summer break is over while your sisters remain here.

1799
01:33:09,220 --> 01:33:09,720
Wait.

1800
01:33:09,720 --> 01:33:11,720
Wait, so just me?

1801
01:33:11,720 --> 01:33:13,720
I don't understand.

1802
01:33:13,720 --> 01:33:15,720
I thought I was special.

1803
01:33:15,720 --> 01:33:19,720
I worked so hard to make sure I had a purpose in this world.

1804
01:33:19,720 --> 01:33:23,720
After all that, how could I end up alone?

1805
01:33:23,720 --> 01:33:26,720
What am I going to do if the others aren't there with me?

1806
01:33:26,720 --> 01:33:29,220
How do I become someone special?

1807
01:33:29,220 --> 01:33:33,220
I don't know where I'm supposed to go from here.

1808
01:33:33,220 --> 01:33:34,720
Wait.

1809
01:33:34,720 --> 01:33:43,720
If Yotsuba has to transfer, then all of us are transferring.

1810
01:33:43,720 --> 01:33:47,220
You're being ridiculous!

1811
01:33:47,220 --> 01:33:49,220
Didn't the rest of you girls pass your exams?

1812
01:33:49,220 --> 01:33:51,720
I passed mine with no trouble.

1813
01:33:51,720 --> 01:33:53,720
But that was only because I cheated.

1814
01:33:53,720 --> 01:33:55,220
What?

1815
01:33:55,220 --> 01:33:57,220
Please tell me that's not true.

1816
01:33:57,220 --> 01:33:58,220
Aww.

1817
01:33:58,220 --> 01:34:00,720
We all did, actually.

1818
01:34:00,720 --> 01:34:01,720
You guys...

1819
01:34:01,720 --> 01:34:02,720
Stop it!

1820
01:34:02,720 --> 01:34:04,720
Why would you do this for me?

1821
01:34:04,720 --> 01:34:09,720
Yotsuba, I don't know what's going on in that thick skull of yours,

1822
01:34:09,720 --> 01:34:12,720
but you're crazy if you think we're going to let you be apart from us!

1823
01:34:12,720 --> 01:34:16,720
We'll all stick together wherever we are.

1824
01:34:16,720 --> 01:34:19,720
Remember, that's what Mom taught us to do.

1825
01:34:22,720 --> 01:34:24,720
Yotsuba, we'll be fine.

1826
01:34:24,720 --> 01:34:27,720
I mean, we're all one-fifth of each other, right?

1827
01:34:27,720 --> 01:34:33,220
So, together, the five of us can get through anything.

1828
01:34:34,220 --> 01:34:37,220
I guess this is what Mom meant when she told me all that stuff.

1829
01:34:39,220 --> 01:34:42,220
I'm going to stop caring about which one of us is the best.

1830
01:34:43,220 --> 01:34:46,220
From now on, I'll live for my sisters.

1831
01:34:46,220 --> 01:34:46,720
My sisters.

1832
01:34:55,720 --> 01:34:57,720
A perfect score?

1833
01:34:57,720 --> 01:35:13,220
My sisters are the only reason I have anything good.

1834
01:35:13,220 --> 01:35:13,720
My memories.

1835
01:35:13,720 --> 01:35:14,720
My feelings.

1836
01:35:14,720 --> 01:35:18,720
I have to forget them.

1837
01:35:18,720 --> 01:35:22,720
You're not hurt, are you?

1838
01:35:22,720 --> 01:35:36,220
You're not hurt, are you?

1839
01:35:36,220 --> 01:35:40,720
All of your sisters are good people, Yotsuba.

1840
01:35:40,720 --> 01:35:41,720
They're amazing.

1841
01:35:41,720 --> 01:35:43,720
I love each one of them.

1842
01:35:43,720 --> 01:35:47,720
I'm really honored that I was able to tutor you guys.

1843
01:35:47,720 --> 01:35:55,220
But still, if you weren't involved, I would have given up a while ago.

1844
01:35:59,220 --> 01:36:01,220
Why would you say something like that?

1845
01:36:01,220 --> 01:36:06,720
I'm a weak human being, and I'll keep tripping up for the rest of my life.

1846
01:36:06,720 --> 01:36:10,220
I know this is rich coming from a loser like me.

1847
01:36:10,220 --> 01:36:16,220
But for all my future screw-ups, I'd be happy if I had you by my side.

1848
01:36:16,220 --> 01:36:19,220
You give me peace.

1849
01:36:19,220 --> 01:36:22,220
Because you're my anchor, Yotsuba.

1850
01:36:22,220 --> 01:36:25,220
And I would love to be that for you.

1851
01:36:25,220 --> 01:36:27,220
So if you hate me, then that's fine.

1852
01:36:27,220 --> 01:36:30,220
But please just tell me how you feel.

1853
01:36:30,220 --> 01:36:36,720
Oh, Asuki, I...

1854
01:36:36,720 --> 01:36:40,720
Tell him.

1855
01:36:40,720 --> 01:36:43,720
Let's put an end to all of this.

1856
01:36:43,720 --> 01:36:45,720
The truth is, I hate you.

1857
01:36:45,720 --> 01:36:46,720
I hate you.

1858
01:36:46,720 --> 01:36:47,720
I hate you.

1859
01:36:47,720 --> 01:36:48,720
I hate you.

1860
01:36:48,720 --> 01:36:50,720
I hate you.

1861
01:36:50,720 --> 01:36:53,720
I love you.

1862
01:36:53,720 --> 01:36:55,720
I do.

1863
01:36:55,720 --> 01:36:59,720
I tried, Asuki, but I can't lie to you.

1864
01:36:59,720 --> 01:37:02,220
I've always loved you.

1865
01:37:10,220 --> 01:37:12,220
I'm sorry about this.

1866
01:37:12,220 --> 01:37:15,220
But there's something I still need to do.

1867
01:37:20,220 --> 01:37:21,220
What?

1868
01:37:21,220 --> 01:37:23,220
You're not dating?

1869
01:37:23,220 --> 01:37:25,220
I guess not.

1870
01:37:25,220 --> 01:37:27,220
Interesting.

1871
01:37:27,220 --> 01:37:29,220
You guys aren't together.

1872
01:37:29,220 --> 01:37:31,720
Which means it's not over yet.

1873
01:37:31,720 --> 01:37:34,720
Futaro technically still doesn't belong to anyone.

1874
01:37:38,720 --> 01:37:39,720
Come on!

1875
01:37:39,720 --> 01:37:40,720
Get it together!

1876
01:37:40,720 --> 01:37:43,720
Yotsuba said she loves you, remember?

1877
01:37:43,720 --> 01:37:44,720
So it's mutual.

1878
01:37:44,720 --> 01:37:47,720
Make a move or she'll start to resent you.

1879
01:37:50,720 --> 01:37:51,720
You're right.

1880
01:37:51,720 --> 01:37:53,220
Thanks, Ichika.

1881
01:37:53,220 --> 01:37:54,220
That helps.

1882
01:37:54,220 --> 01:38:04,220
Even if you were the one he ended up choosing, I would still be happy for you.

1883
01:38:04,220 --> 01:38:08,220
I didn't understand Nino then, but I get it now.

1884
01:38:08,220 --> 01:38:12,720
You knew I liked Fu long before what happened yesterday.

1885
01:38:12,720 --> 01:38:15,720
You've known how I felt about him from the beginning.

1886
01:38:15,720 --> 01:38:18,720
That's why I don't want you to be worried about me anymore.

1887
01:38:18,720 --> 01:38:20,720
Nino, you're my sister.

1888
01:38:20,720 --> 01:38:22,720
How can I not be worried about you?

1889
01:38:22,720 --> 01:38:24,720
Alright, fine.

1890
01:38:24,720 --> 01:38:26,720
Then I guess things are over between us.

1891
01:38:26,720 --> 01:38:29,720
If this is how you insist it has to be,

1892
01:38:29,720 --> 01:38:34,220
then from now on, you're not my sister.

1893
01:38:39,220 --> 01:38:40,220
Yotsuba.

1894
01:38:40,220 --> 01:38:41,220
Huh?

1895
01:38:41,220 --> 01:38:44,220
You should go inside soon or you're going to catch a cold.

1896
01:38:44,220 --> 01:38:45,220
Miku.

1897
01:38:45,220 --> 01:38:47,220
Yotsuba, actually.

1898
01:38:47,220 --> 01:38:49,720
My name is Yotsuba.

1899
01:38:49,720 --> 01:38:51,720
What's this about?

1900
01:38:51,720 --> 01:38:54,720
I was thinking,

1901
01:38:54,720 --> 01:38:56,720
if Futuro didn't choose me,

1902
01:38:56,720 --> 01:38:58,720
then I would become you.

1903
01:38:58,720 --> 01:39:00,720
So I could be with him instead.

1904
01:39:00,720 --> 01:39:03,720
What do you think?

1905
01:39:09,720 --> 01:39:11,720
I don't think that's right.

1906
01:39:11,720 --> 01:39:13,720
It just isn't.

1907
01:39:13,720 --> 01:39:19,220
It's cold.

1908
01:39:19,220 --> 01:39:21,220
Do you want to go talk somewhere else?

1909
01:39:24,220 --> 01:39:25,220
Wow.

1910
01:39:25,220 --> 01:39:27,220
Karaoke with only the two of us.

1911
01:39:27,220 --> 01:39:29,220
This is a first, huh?

1912
01:39:33,220 --> 01:39:35,220
Yotsuba?

1913
01:39:35,220 --> 01:39:36,220
Yeah?

1914
01:39:36,220 --> 01:39:37,220
What's up?

1915
01:39:37,220 --> 01:39:38,220
It was a joke.

1916
01:39:38,220 --> 01:39:42,220
I didn't mean all that stuff I said about trying to become you.

1917
01:39:42,220 --> 01:39:45,720
Obviously, I can pretend I'm you,

1918
01:39:45,720 --> 01:39:47,720
but I can't be you.

1919
01:39:47,720 --> 01:39:50,720
For one thing, this juice is way too sweet for me.

1920
01:39:50,720 --> 01:39:51,720
Look.

1921
01:39:51,720 --> 01:39:53,720
I'm still mad at you, though.

1922
01:39:53,720 --> 01:39:58,720
Because I would never do anything to hurt Futuro the way you are right now.

1923
01:39:58,720 --> 01:40:02,720
I can tell you're having a hard time figuring out what you want.

1924
01:40:02,720 --> 01:40:06,720
If you like him so much, why is it such a difficult decision to make?

1925
01:40:06,720 --> 01:40:08,220
It isn't that.

1926
01:40:08,220 --> 01:40:12,220
I've had these feelings for Uasuki for a really long time.

1927
01:40:12,220 --> 01:40:15,220
And they haven't changed, not even a little bit.

1928
01:40:15,220 --> 01:40:18,220
That makes even less sense.

1929
01:40:18,220 --> 01:40:20,220
You have no good reason to hesitate.

1930
01:40:20,220 --> 01:40:24,220
Unless you're still hung up on what happened back at our other school.

1931
01:40:24,220 --> 01:40:29,720
You should stop worrying about all of us.

1932
01:40:29,720 --> 01:40:31,720
Go out with him.

1933
01:40:33,720 --> 01:40:36,720
Did that sound like I meant it?

1934
01:40:36,720 --> 01:40:39,720
I figured it would turn out this way.

1935
01:40:39,720 --> 01:40:42,720
But still, I can't deny that it hurts me.

1936
01:40:42,720 --> 01:40:46,720
It's just hard to keep my feelings in check.

1937
01:40:46,720 --> 01:40:48,720
Because I care so much.

1938
01:40:48,720 --> 01:40:55,220
So, if we accept how you feel, then you should do the same for us.

1939
01:40:55,220 --> 01:40:56,220
This isn't easy.

1940
01:40:58,220 --> 01:41:00,220
I should have been more careful.

1941
01:41:00,220 --> 01:41:03,220
I didn't consider what Nino was going through.

1942
01:41:03,220 --> 01:41:06,220
No wonder she's angry at me.

1943
01:41:06,220 --> 01:41:12,220
Nino told me once that in love, we may not be allies, but we're not enemies either.

1944
01:41:12,220 --> 01:41:13,220
Yeah.

1945
01:41:13,220 --> 01:41:19,720
Okay, now that we both agree on that, I'll battle you my way.

1946
01:41:19,720 --> 01:41:23,720
And my strategy is simply not to encourage you.

1947
01:41:27,720 --> 01:41:29,720
We might as well sing.

1948
01:41:29,720 --> 01:41:30,720
Sounds fun.

1949
01:41:30,720 --> 01:41:31,720
Get ready.

1950
01:41:31,720 --> 01:41:33,720
Cause I'm gonna sing a whole lot better than you.

1951
01:41:33,720 --> 01:41:35,720
That's what you think.

1952
01:41:35,720 --> 01:41:40,720
Hey, look!

1953
01:41:40,720 --> 01:41:42,720
The weather's so nice!

1954
01:41:42,720 --> 01:41:47,220
I know it was my idea to sing, but I didn't expect to be here for the whole night.

1955
01:41:47,220 --> 01:41:50,220
Hey, Miku.

1956
01:41:50,220 --> 01:41:52,220
Let's go home.

1957
01:41:52,220 --> 01:41:54,220
To our sisters.

1958
01:41:57,220 --> 01:42:00,220
Yotsuba's mistaken about one thing.

1959
01:42:00,220 --> 01:42:05,220
Then again, I'm probably never going to tell her what I really think.

1960
01:42:05,220 --> 01:42:08,220
If my sisters and I had never transferred to this school,

1961
01:42:08,220 --> 01:42:11,220
then Futura wouldn't have walked into our lives.

1962
01:42:11,220 --> 01:42:17,720
When you look at it that way, it's hard to see it as a negative.

1963
01:42:17,720 --> 01:42:21,720
It's because I met him.

1964
01:42:21,720 --> 01:42:25,720
That I...

1965
01:42:25,720 --> 01:42:27,720
We should go.

1966
01:42:27,720 --> 01:42:30,220
I couldn't become Yotsuba.

1967
01:42:30,220 --> 01:42:34,220
But the truth is, Yotsuba could never be me either.

1968
01:42:34,220 --> 01:42:36,220
I couldn't wrap my head around that at first.

1969
01:42:36,220 --> 01:42:40,220
But now, I finally like myself enough to believe it.

1970
01:42:42,220 --> 01:42:43,220
Itsuki.

1971
01:42:44,220 --> 01:42:45,220
You got a minute?

1972
01:42:45,220 --> 01:42:47,720
Um, sure, what is it?

1973
01:42:47,720 --> 01:42:49,720
There's something I want to talk about.

1974
01:42:49,720 --> 01:42:51,720
Somewhere more private?

1975
01:42:51,720 --> 01:42:53,220
More private?

1976
01:42:53,220 --> 01:42:54,220
Okay then.

1977
01:42:54,220 --> 01:42:55,220
In here.

1978
01:42:59,220 --> 01:43:00,220
So...

1979
01:43:00,220 --> 01:43:02,220
What's up, Uesugi?

1980
01:43:02,220 --> 01:43:03,220
Here?

1981
01:43:09,220 --> 01:43:11,220
Oh no, I'm so sorry.

1982
01:43:11,220 --> 01:43:13,220
It's okay.

1983
01:43:13,220 --> 01:43:13,720
Carrie.

1984
01:43:13,720 --> 01:43:15,720
I don't understand.

1985
01:43:15,720 --> 01:43:17,720
Why am I still so uneasy?

1986
01:43:17,720 --> 01:43:19,720
This place looks handy.

1987
01:43:19,720 --> 01:43:28,220
You're the one who drove a wedge between the five of us.

1988
01:43:28,220 --> 01:43:31,220
You know that, don't you?

1989
01:43:31,220 --> 01:43:33,220
What I did was selfish.

1990
01:43:33,220 --> 01:43:36,220
I'm sorry for not respecting your feelings.

1991
01:43:36,220 --> 01:43:38,220
I was being too pushy.

1992
01:43:38,220 --> 01:43:42,220
But still, it doesn't change how I feel about it.

1993
01:43:42,220 --> 01:43:43,720
And what I wish for.

1994
01:43:43,720 --> 01:43:44,720
Oh, save it.

1995
01:43:44,720 --> 01:43:47,220
I know you still expect to be coddled.

1996
01:43:47,220 --> 01:43:48,720
I'll never approve of.

1997
01:43:51,720 --> 01:43:53,720
Oh, it's just some mice.

1998
01:43:53,720 --> 01:43:54,720
Yeah, sure.

1999
01:43:54,720 --> 01:43:55,720
Mice.

2000
01:43:55,720 --> 01:43:57,720
That was close.

2001
01:43:57,720 --> 01:43:59,720
You think it's too risky to go for the door?

2002
01:43:59,720 --> 01:44:02,720
I don't know, but could you give me some space?

2003
01:44:02,720 --> 01:44:05,720
It's going to look really bad if those two see us like this.

2004
01:44:05,720 --> 01:44:08,720
Anyway, lunch break is almost over.

2005
01:44:08,720 --> 01:44:09,720
Let's go back.

2006
01:44:09,720 --> 01:44:10,720
Hold on!

2007
01:44:11,720 --> 01:44:12,720
What?

2008
01:44:12,720 --> 01:44:18,220
I gathered up all of my courage to tell you this.

2009
01:44:18,220 --> 01:44:22,220
What I want most is for you to approve of me dating Uesugi.

2010
01:44:22,220 --> 01:44:23,220
I just told you.

2011
01:44:23,220 --> 01:44:24,220
Listen!

2012
01:44:24,220 --> 01:44:26,220
It doesn't have to be right now.

2013
01:44:26,220 --> 01:44:29,220
It could be months or years.

2014
01:44:29,220 --> 01:44:32,220
I don't know how long it'll take you to change your mind.

2015
01:44:32,220 --> 01:44:36,720
But eventually, I want you to understand and accept how much I love Uesugi.

2016
01:44:36,720 --> 01:44:40,720
My love for him is just as strong as yours.

2017
01:44:40,720 --> 01:44:42,720
You're right.

2018
01:44:42,720 --> 01:44:46,720
Even if you apologized or tried everything in the world to convince me,

2019
01:44:46,720 --> 01:44:49,720
we both know I wouldn't buy it at all.

2020
01:44:49,720 --> 01:44:54,720
And yet, in spite of that, you're still dead set on going down such a painful path?

2021
01:44:54,720 --> 01:44:56,220
Yes, Nino.

2022
01:44:56,220 --> 01:44:58,720
I love him and you guys with all my heart.

2023
01:44:58,720 --> 01:45:01,220
And nothing's going to change that.

2024
01:45:01,220 --> 01:45:04,220
Honestly, that's stupid.

2025
01:45:04,220 --> 01:45:06,220
But it sounds like something you'd say.

2026
01:45:10,220 --> 01:45:13,220
There are certain shackles that come with being a quintuplet.

2027
01:45:13,220 --> 01:45:18,220
And when I saw you step out of them, I was jealous of you.

2028
01:45:19,220 --> 01:45:24,220
After all that we've been through, do you still think of me as someone to compete with?

2029
01:45:24,220 --> 01:45:25,720
Of course I do.

2030
01:45:25,720 --> 01:45:29,720
We're sisters, which means we'll always be aware of what's going on with each other.

2031
01:45:29,720 --> 01:45:31,720
Sometimes as friends.

2032
01:45:31,720 --> 01:45:32,720
Sometimes foes.

2033
01:45:32,720 --> 01:45:33,720
We're like...

2034
01:45:33,720 --> 01:45:34,720
I get it.

2035
01:45:34,720 --> 01:45:35,720
Rivals.

2036
01:45:37,720 --> 01:45:39,720
Well, this battle isn't over yet.

2037
01:45:39,720 --> 01:45:42,720
Because I'll be observing your relationship with him from a distance.

2038
01:45:42,720 --> 01:45:45,720
You show even the slightest weakness.

2039
01:45:45,720 --> 01:45:47,720
And I'll come to take him away from you.

2040
01:45:49,720 --> 01:45:50,720
Right.

2041
01:45:52,720 --> 01:45:53,720
That's all I wanted to say.

2042
01:45:54,720 --> 01:45:56,720
You can come out now, you little rats.

2043
01:45:58,220 --> 01:45:59,720
You knew the whole time?

2044
01:46:00,720 --> 01:46:01,720
They can explain.

2045
01:46:02,220 --> 01:46:03,720
You were here too?

2046
01:46:03,720 --> 01:46:04,720
For how long?

2047
01:46:04,720 --> 01:46:06,720
Please don't tell me you heard everything.

2048
01:46:06,720 --> 01:46:07,720
Sorry.

2049
01:46:10,720 --> 01:46:12,720
I hope you heard what I said, Fu.

2050
01:46:13,720 --> 01:46:15,220
I meant every word.

2051
01:46:15,220 --> 01:46:17,720
Keep your guard up or it's all over.

2052
01:46:17,720 --> 01:46:18,220
Okay.

2053
01:46:18,220 --> 01:46:20,220
I'll try to remember that.

2054
01:46:20,220 --> 01:46:24,220
You sure got yourself involved with a crazy group of siblings.

2055
01:46:24,220 --> 01:46:27,220
But I think I can finally say this now.

2056
01:46:27,220 --> 01:46:30,220
You're not alone.

2057
01:46:30,220 --> 01:46:32,220
You never will be.

2058
01:46:32,220 --> 01:46:33,720
Congratulations, Iwasuki.

2059
01:46:33,720 --> 01:46:34,720
Um...

2060
01:46:34,720 --> 01:46:35,720
Listen.

2061
01:46:35,720 --> 01:46:50,220
I just wanted to say that I appreciate you inviting me out today.

2062
01:46:50,220 --> 01:46:52,720
Sorry to steal your day off.

2063
01:46:52,720 --> 01:46:53,720
No.

2064
01:46:53,720 --> 01:46:54,720
I'm glad.

2065
01:46:54,720 --> 01:46:55,720
It'll be fun.

2066
01:46:55,720 --> 01:46:56,720
You think so?

2067
01:47:00,720 --> 01:47:04,720
I just figured it's kind of hard to find time to be alone during school.

2068
01:47:04,720 --> 01:47:07,220
That's true.

2069
01:47:07,220 --> 01:47:09,220
Especially since my sisters are always around.

2070
01:47:14,220 --> 01:47:17,220
The train has stopped due to obstacles on the track.

2071
01:47:17,220 --> 01:47:18,220
We deeply apologize for the...

2072
01:47:18,220 --> 01:47:20,220
This seems backwards.

2073
01:47:20,220 --> 01:47:21,220
I guess so.

2074
01:47:21,220 --> 01:47:22,220
Yeah.

2075
01:47:22,220 --> 01:47:26,720
Please, feel free to order as much food as you want.

2076
01:47:26,720 --> 01:47:27,720
Everything's on me.

2077
01:47:27,720 --> 01:47:28,720
Yay!

2078
01:47:28,720 --> 01:47:29,720
Mmm, it's yummy.

2079
01:47:29,720 --> 01:47:31,720
I'm glad you like it.

2080
01:47:31,720 --> 01:47:33,720
This is embarrassing.

2081
01:47:33,720 --> 01:47:36,720
Who goes to a family restaurant on a first date?

2082
01:47:36,720 --> 01:47:38,720
I think it's kind of endearing.

2083
01:47:38,720 --> 01:47:41,720
Coupons, too?

2084
01:47:41,720 --> 01:47:42,720
Is that bad?

2085
01:47:42,720 --> 01:47:45,720
It's so tacky to use coupons on a date.

2086
01:47:45,720 --> 01:47:48,720
Say what you want, but he's obviously trying his best.

2087
01:47:48,720 --> 01:47:51,720
You're hoping for a referral to a sports universe.

2088
01:47:51,720 --> 01:47:53,220
University, right?

2089
01:47:53,220 --> 01:47:54,220
Uh-huh.

2090
01:47:54,220 --> 01:47:57,220
You could do a lot of different things with that.

2091
01:47:57,220 --> 01:48:00,220
Is it your dream to become a professional athlete?

2092
01:48:00,220 --> 01:48:01,220
No.

2093
01:48:01,220 --> 01:48:04,220
To be honest, I don't remember what I wanted to be as a kid.

2094
01:48:04,220 --> 01:48:08,220
It's been so long, but one thing I do know is that I'm really in my element when

2095
01:48:08,220 --> 01:48:10,220
I'm supporting other people.

2096
01:48:10,220 --> 01:48:12,220
It happened because I gave up on something.

2097
01:48:12,220 --> 01:48:16,220
But then I realized it was part of myself I could be proud of.

2098
01:48:16,220 --> 01:48:17,220
Yeah.

2099
01:48:17,220 --> 01:48:18,220
It sounds like you.

2100
01:48:18,220 --> 01:48:20,220
I have you to thank.

2101
01:48:20,220 --> 01:48:22,720
You're the reason I figured that out.

2102
01:48:22,720 --> 01:48:23,720
What?

2103
01:48:23,720 --> 01:48:24,720
Really?

2104
01:48:24,720 --> 01:48:25,720
Of course.

2105
01:48:25,720 --> 01:48:26,720
Uh...

2106
01:48:26,720 --> 01:48:32,720
Anyway, if I do get into university somewhere, then that's probably the kind of career I

2107
01:48:32,720 --> 01:48:33,720
